Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.74,0:00:37.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一个看似充满魔法的时代……
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.42,0:00:41.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一张面孔……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}A face...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.59,0:00:45.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一支舰队……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}...a fleet...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.46,0:00:49.55,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一场战争……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}...a War...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.26,0:00:54.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一个男人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}...a Man...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.64,0:00:59.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一个念头……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}...a thought...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.19,0:01:03.15,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一条计策……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}...a trick...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.23,0:01:08.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一条攻破特洛伊城墙的计策\N{\rEN\blur0.8}...a trick to break the walls of Troy.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.11,0:01:13.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}让特洛伊在哀号中化为灰烬！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And burn it screaming to the ground!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.38,0:02:06.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这是什么意思？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What does it mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.30,0:02:16.55,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一份礼物\N{\rEN\blur0.8}A gift.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.72,0:02:21.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}献给雅典娜的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}For Athena.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.10,0:02:25.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们信奉同样的神\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Common gods.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.23,0:02:27.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}要尊重他们的供奉\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Respect their offering.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.82,0:02:32.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}别让海浪把它卷走！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Save it from the waves!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.36,0:02:35.03,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}把它送到雅典娜神庙\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Take it to Athena's temple.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.86,0:02:37.32,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}战争结束了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The war is over.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.62,0:02:45.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一张面孔……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}A face...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.25,0:02:50.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一支舰队……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}...a fleet...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.88,0:02:54.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一场战争……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}...a war...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.22,0:02:58.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一个男人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}...2 man...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.80,0:02:59.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}停下！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Sfop/
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.39,0:03:05.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}别唱这首\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Not this song.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.36,0:03:12.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}妈妈的乖宝宝！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Mommy's boy!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.73,0:03:14.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}跑吧 跑吧 小男子汉！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Run, run, little man!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.49,0:03:16.49,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}快跑！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Run!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.53,0:03:19.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我想提醒他们 喝的是谁家的酒\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I wanna remind them of whose wine they're drinking.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.99,0:03:21.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我不要歌里的奥德修斯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't want Odysseus' song.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.87,0:03:22.95,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我要他本人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I want Odysseus.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.04,0:03:24.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那你为什么夜夜招待求婚者\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Then why do you entertain suitors
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.58,0:03:26.04,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}让他们待在他的家里？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}in his house night after night?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.79,0:03:30.96,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这世上 男人可以随心所欲\N{\rEN\blur0.8}In this world, a man does what he chooses.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.04,0:03:32.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我只能尽力而为\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I do what I can.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.21,0:03:34.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我已经是男人了 母亲\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I am aman now, Mom.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.01,0:03:36.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那就把他们赶出去\N{\rEN\blur0.8}So throw them out.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.76,0:03:39.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}违背宙斯的律法 看他们会怎么对你\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Break Zeus' Law and see what they do to you
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.59,0:03:41.05,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}只要你给了他们这个借口\N{\rEN\blur0.8}if you give them that excuse.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.85,0:03:49.27,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我已经失去了丈夫\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I've already lost a husband.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.35,0:03:51.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不想再失去儿子\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't wanna lose a son.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.15,0:03:52.32,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可父亲会回来的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But Dad's coming back.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.40,0:03:53.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那他在哪儿？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Then where is he?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.98,0:03:56.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}特洛伊陷落 已经八年了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Eight years since Troy fell.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.03,0:03:58.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他离开我们快二十年了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Almost 20 since he left us.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.95,0:03:59.99,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他在哪儿？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Where is he?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.67,0:04:14.04,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们得像当初欢迎各位一样欢迎他\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We have to welcome him like we welcomed all of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.13,0:04:15.42,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你把我们当乞写？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Are you calling us beggars?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.50,0:04:18.05,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是说 我们已款待各位三年\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm saying you've been welcome here for three years.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.13,0:04:21.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们之所以叨扰这么久\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We've only enjoyed your hospitality for so long,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.93,0:04:24.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是因为你母亲迟迟不肯选\N{\rEN\blur0.8}because your mother won't choose.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.06,0:04:26.27,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}她早就嫁人了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}She's already married.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.35,0:04:27.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}奥德修斯死了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Odysseus is dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.48,0:04:30.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我父亲的事 你知道什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What do you know about my dad?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.69,0:04:34.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我知道他养的牛又老又柴\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I know he kept stringy cattle
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.15,0:04:35.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}酿的酒也难喝\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-and bad wine.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.73,0:04:38.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}头两年 好的都被你们吃喝光了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You had the best of it the first two seasons.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.36,0:04:39.95,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我还知道 他再也没回来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And I know he never came home.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.03,0:04:41.32,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}只是暂时没回\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Not yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.91,0:04:46.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你连父亲都不认识 还苦苦盼着他\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You're pining for a daddy you didn't even know.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.62,0:04:48.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}活像个哭鼻子的野种\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Like some sniveling bastard.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.70,0:04:51.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}既然谁也不能确定亲爹是谁\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, since none of us can really know who our fathers are,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.79,0:04:53.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你就别装作了解我父亲\N{\rEN\blur0.8}don't claim to know mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.46,0:04:54.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可我确实认识他\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But I did know him.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.67,0:04:57.42,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}小时候 我们看过他打猎\N{\rEN\blur0.8}As boys. We watched him hunt.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.51,0:05:01.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他远征特洛伊时 我曾自愿参军\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I tried to volunteer for his expedition to Troy,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.72,0:05:03.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可他叫我留下\N{\rEN\blur0.8}but he told me to stay here
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.30,0:05:04.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}照看你\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and keep an eye on you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.68,0:05:06.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}照看我 还是我母亲？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-On me, or my mother?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.02,0:05:09.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}看看总不犯法吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You can't blame me for looking.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.73,0:05:11.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我父亲会回来的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}My dad is coming home.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.10,0:05:13.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他待客 可不会像她这么客气\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And his hospitality won't be as generous as hers.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.02,0:05:16.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这么说 他不守宙斯的律法？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}So he doesn't follow Zeus' Law, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.11,0:05:19.03,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}宙斯教我们 将心比心款待陌生人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Zeus' Law tells us to treat strangers as we'd be treated
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.11,0:05:21.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}因为他们可能是神明的化身\N{\rEN\blur0.8}because they might be gods in disguise.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.90,0:05:24.53,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}安提诺俄斯 我们已确定你不是神\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I think we've established, Antinous, that you are not a god.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.83,0:05:27.79,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这位闻着可一点也不像神\N{\rEN\blur0.8}This one certainly doesn't smell like a god.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.87,0:05:29.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}闻着像神 还算什么伪装\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Wouldn't be much of a disguise if he did.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.58,0:05:30.96,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}当心\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Careful.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.46,0:05:33.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他也许现在就会劈死你\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He might strike you down. Right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.63,0:05:40.97,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}走吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.47,0:05:49.31,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那声雷只是巧合\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That thunder was luck.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.06,0:05:52.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}未必 你的眼睛透着智慧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't know. You have wise eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.98,0:05:55.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}像雅典娜的眼睛 来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Athena's eyes. Here.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.56,0:05:57.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你搭商船来的？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You sailed with traders?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.52,0:05:58.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}从斯巴达来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}From Sparta.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.02,0:06:00.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}墨涅拉俄斯打完仗回家了吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Has Menelaus come home from the war?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.99,0:06:04.99,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}几年前就回了 奥德修斯还没回来？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Years ago. Odysseus never came back?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.07,0:06:06.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们连他是死是活都不知道\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We don't even know if he's alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.37,0:06:07.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你听说过什么吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Have you heard anything?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.49,0:06:09.29,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}只听过歌里唱他如何赢得战争\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The song of how he won the war.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.37,0:06:10.95,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那个谁都听过 还有别的吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We've all heard that. Anything else?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.45,0:06:12.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没有\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.21,0:06:17.79,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可斯巴达到处都是特洛伊之战的老兵\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But Sparta is full of Trojan War veterans.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.88,0:06:19.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}总有人知道些什么\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Someone'll know something.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.88,0:06:23.47,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你是奥德修斯的儿子？ 去去斯巴达吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You're Odysseus' son? Go to Sparta.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.55,0:06:26.05,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}去见墨涅拉俄斯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Go. See Menelaus.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.72,0:06:27.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他会欢迎你\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He'd welcome you.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.85,0:06:31.93,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}王后要见这位异乡人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The Queen wants to speak to the stranger.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.44,0:06:35.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}她就靠这些消息活着\N{\rEN\blur0.8}She lives for news.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.98,0:06:39.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}但别给她虚假的希望\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Just don't try to give her any false hope.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.57,0:06:40.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}她自有办法辨别\N{\rEN\blur0.8}She has some way of knowing
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.90,0:06:43.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一个人是否真的见过奥德修斯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}whether a person has actually seen Odysseus.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.36,0:06:44.53,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}看见那个人了吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You see that man?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.61,0:06:46.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他虽已看不清 却仍能\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He can't see much anymore, but that doesn't stop him
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.78,0:06:48.45,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}把旅人活活打死\N{\rEN\blur0.8}beating travelers to death
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.53,0:06:50.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}只因他们编造我父亲的消息\N{\rEN\blur0.8}in exchange for lies about my father.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.48,0:07:19.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不 不 太快了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-No, no, too fast.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.44,0:07:21.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你怎么知道？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}How can you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.61,0:07:25.11,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}听招式的节奏就够了 不必用眼睛\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You don't need eyes to hear a hasty combination.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.20,0:07:26.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}门托尔 逼紧点\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Mentor, push him.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.83,0:07:36.04,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不 不 太快了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No, no. Too fast.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.72,0:07:47.05,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他跟你一样不友好\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He's as friendly as you.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.13,0:07:49.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他只听你父亲的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He only answered to your father.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.97,0:07:51.55,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}父亲从哪儿弄来的？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Where'd he get him from?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.64,0:07:53.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们就在这里相遇\N{\rEN\blur0.8}They met right here.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.43,0:07:55.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Ah.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.56,0:08:00.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}来吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.06,0:08:02.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rEN\blur0.8}Aw.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.73,0:08:03.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我要这只\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'll take him.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.07,0:08:05.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}给你儿子？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}For your boy?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.15,0:08:06.49,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}当猎犬\N{\rEN\blur0.8}For a hunting dog.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.32,0:08:09.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还真让他说中了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Damned if he wasn't right.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.15,0:08:47.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}别动 想留多大的疤？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Hold still. How bad a scar do you want?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.61,0:08:51.45,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你为什么总要拨一下弓弦？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Why do you always pluck your bow?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.53,0:08:52.53,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这样才公平\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's only fair.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.62,0:08:54.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}提醒你的猎物？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}To warn your prey?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.49,0:08:55.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}战斗也要讲荣誉\N{\rEN\blur0.8}To fight with honor.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.66,0:08:57.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可你是在狩猎 又不是打仗\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But you weren't fighting. You were hunting.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.62,0:08:59.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}狩猎不过是隐蔽的战斗\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Ah, hunting's nothing but fighting with stealth.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.04,0:09:01.29,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}聪明\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Clever.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.37,0:09:04.04,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}聪明 可你早晚会聪明反被聪明误\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Clever, but your cleverness gonna get you in trouble.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.13,0:09:05.09,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}再来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Try again.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.79,0:09:08.05,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这次别那么快 别那么精准\N{\rEN\blur0.8}This time, not as fast or precise.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.13,0:09:10.67,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一味严防死守 赢不了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You can't win with a perfect defense.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.76,0:09:11.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}诱敌出招\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Draw the attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.97,0:09:13.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-怎么诱？  -迟疑一下\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-How?   -Hesitate.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.93,0:09:16.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}把腹部的空当留给对方\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Open your belly to your opponent's blade.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.60,0:09:18.27,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他的进攻 就成了你的机会\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Their attack becomes your chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.17,0:09:51.63,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你也这样教过我父亲？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You teach my father that?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.72,0:09:54.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不 是他教我的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No, no, he taught me.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.38,0:09:56.14,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他说 你不可能永远\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He said, "You're not always
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.22,0:09:58.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}比别人更强壮 更敏捷\N{\rEN\blur0.8}going to be the strongest or the fastest,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.60,0:10:01.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}所以 要比别人更聪明\N{\rEN\blur0.8}so be... Be the smartest."
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.73,0:10:03.14,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}换作他 他会怎么办？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What would he do, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.23,0:10:05.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}回来发现家里全是求婚者呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}If he came back here to find all these suitors in his house?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.73,0:10:09.15,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}别说了 我都不敢想他会怎么收拾他们\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Don't. I can't even let myself imagine what he'd do to them.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.23,0:10:10.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们人太多了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}There are so many.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.86,0:10:13.03,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}砍倒几个 其他人就怂了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Cut a couple down, the others cave.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.11,0:10:15.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}都是欺软怕硬的懦夫\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Bullies and cowards.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.16,0:10:16.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}多数人当年都够年纪去特洛伊\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Most of them were old enough to go to Troy,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.87,0:10:18.49,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可一看到阿伽门农的船帆·\N{\rEN\blur0.8}but when they saw Agamemnon's sail...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.33,0:10:23.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们的父亲就把他们藏起来了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}...their fathers hid them.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.34,0:10:28.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他知道 阿伽门农这场战争\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And he knew Agamemnon's war
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.92,0:10:31.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}会耗费许多年 夺去许多性命\N{\rEN\blur0.8}would take many years and many lives.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.26,0:10:38.55,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}所以他用抽签来征兵\N{\rEN\blur0.8}So he raised his army by lottery.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.43,0:10:42.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-名字？  -西农\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Name?   -Sinon.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.56,0:10:44.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}抽吧 不用去\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Draw. No.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.43,0:10:45.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-名字？  -安提诺俄斯：\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Name?   -Antinous.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.77,0:10:46.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}抽吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Draw.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.40,0:10:49.32,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}要去\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.40,0:10:50.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}抽签？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}By lots?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.24,0:10:55.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}安提诺俄斯说他是自愿的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Antinous told me he volunteered.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.49,0:10:57.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我看他们在打什么主意\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I think they're up to something.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.54,0:11:07.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你儿子想顶替西农\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Your boy's trying to take Sinon's place.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.50,0:11:09.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我不会让他去\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm not gonna let him.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.00,0:11:11.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他得留下 照顾家人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He needs to stay here. Take care of his family.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.88,0:11:16.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他也能照看你儿子\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He can watch over your boy too.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.34,0:11:17.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}当然\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.51,0:11:22.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他跟我走\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He's with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.10,0:11:25.31,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他想让安提诺俄斯照顾我？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He wanted Antinous to look after me?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.39,0:11:26.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不 不\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No, no, no.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.94,0:11:29.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}奥德修斯只是体谅为父者的羞愧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But Odysseus was sensitive to a father's shame.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.73,0:11:31.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他同情那些父亲\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He felt for these fathers.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.48,0:11:34.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}比起荣耀 他更看重你和你母亲\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You and your mother meant more to him than promises of glory.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.11,0:11:37.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}所以他早知道要离开多年\N{\rEN\blur0.8}So he knew it would be years.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.91,0:11:40.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他告诉我母亲了吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Did he tell my mother?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.70,0:11:42.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这得问她\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's a question for her.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.20,0:11:45.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}欧迈俄斯 他到底还回不回来？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Eumaeus, is he ever coming back?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.79,0:11:48.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}阿尔戈斯觉得会\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Argus thinks so.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.17,0:11:50.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我从没见过狗能活到二十岁\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Never known a dog reach 20.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.67,0:11:52.96,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可他的主人早就不在人世了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But he's long outlived his master.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.27,0:12:11.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我不是来打扰你的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I didn't mean to stop you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.90,0:12:16.36,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我不赶时间\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm in no hurry.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.44,0:12:20.74,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}长老们说 等我织好你祖父的裹尸布\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The elders decreed when I finish your grandfather's burial shroud,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.82,0:12:22.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就该改嫁了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}it'll be time to remarry.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.28,0:12:23.33,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}为什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.04,0:12:31.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}伊萨卡太久没有国王了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Ithaca's been without a king too long.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.83,0:12:33.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们想求个安稳\N{\rEN\blur0.8}They want security.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.34,0:12:34.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}怕什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}From what?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.42,0:12:36.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}海上来的民族\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The people from the sea.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.46,0:12:38.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那只是旅人的传言\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's just traveler's tales.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.80,0:12:40.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们对外界的了解 全全靠旅人的传言\N{\rEN\blur0.8}All we know of the world is traveler's tales.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.72,0:12:42.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}特洛伊陷落的消息也是这样传来的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's how we found out Troy had fallen.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.10,0:12:44.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}如今人人都在说\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now they all tell stories
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.43,0:12:46.47,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}海上来的民族四处劫掠\N{\rEN\blur0.8}of attacks by people from the sea.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.56,0:12:49.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那些海上来的人是谁？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And who are the people from the sea?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.52,0:12:52.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没人知道 可长老们要伊萨卡有所防备\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No one knows, but the elders want Ithaca to be prepared.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.73,0:12:53.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}防备？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Prepared?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.86,0:12:56.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们属于世上最伟大的文明\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We're part of the greatest civilization ever known.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.44,0:13:00.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}看看这座宏伟的宫殿\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Look at this great house.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.15,0:13:01.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这些石头和人类的智慧一样古老\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Stones as old as knowledge.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.99,0:13:05.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}却任由一群贪婪的不速之客摆布？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}At the mercy of some greedy, unwanted guests?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.78,0:13:07.79,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}人们若不再尊重它的意义\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The structure's nothing
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.70,0:13:10.33,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这座建筑就一文不值\N{\rEN\blur0.8}without people's respect for its meaning.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.08,0:13:12.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}宙斯的律法\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Zeus' Law.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.08,0:13:15.09,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}将心比心 以礼待人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Treat others as you would be treated.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.17,0:13:18.17,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们践踏律法 就会毁掉一切\N{\rEN\blur0.8}They abuse that, they destroy everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.26,0:13:20.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那你怎么还想嫁给他们？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}So how could you think of marrying one of them?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.01,0:13:23.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}因为很久以前\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Because, a long time ago,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.76,0:13:26.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你父亲就要我这样做\N{\rEN\blur0.8}your father asked me to.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.97,0:13:28.47,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}阿伽门农是我们的王\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Agamemnon is our king.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.56,0:13:31.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}特洛伊人抢走了他弟弟的妻子\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And the Trojans took his brother's wife.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.18,0:13:33.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也可能是她自愿跟人私奔\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Or she ran away with them.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.31,0:13:36.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}都一样 据说特洛伊城墙坚不可摧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Either way. The walls of Troy are said to be impregnable.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.94,0:13:40.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们会围在城外\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And we'll sit outside that great city,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.53,0:13:42.32,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}设法引他们出城迎战\N{\rEN\blur0.8}trying to draw them into battle.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.36,0:13:47.33,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一晃多年过去 忒勒马科斯长大\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Then years go by. And Telemachus grows.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.95,0:13:50.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你也习惯了没有我的日子\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And you learn life without me.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.16,0:13:52.87,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}墨涅拉俄斯终究会放弃海伦\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Menelaus will give up on Helen.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.30,0:13:59.17,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可阿伽门农只是借机\N{\rEN\blur0.8}This is Agamemnon's excuse
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.26,0:14:02.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}打破特洛伊对商路的控制\N{\rEN\blur0.8}to break Troy's control of the trading routes.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.47,0:14:07.76,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他绝不会放弃这个机会\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He won't let it pass. Ever.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.48,0:14:16.73,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}要是你拒绝呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, what if you refuse?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.49,0:14:24.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他就会带走我们的儿子\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He'll take our son.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.70,0:14:27.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他不会的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He would never.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.20,0:14:29.33,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他连亲生女儿都拿去献祭\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He sacrificed his own daughter.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.41,0:14:31.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}只为求一个顺风\N{\rEN\blur0.8}For favorable winds.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.50,0:14:34.87,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}神明为什么会要他女儿的命？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Why would the gods want his daughter's life'?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.50,0:14:37.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}献祭的力量\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The power of a sacrifice
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.84,0:14:41.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就在于献祭者付出的代价\N{\rEN\blur0.8}is in the cost to the person making it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.80,0:14:46.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}简直丧心病狂\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's monstrous.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.06,0:14:50.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也说明他志在必得\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And committed.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.48,0:14:55.31,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我短期内回不来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I won't return soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.27,0:14:57.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}甚至可能再也不回\N{\rEN\blur0.8}If at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.94,0:15:03.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不如我们逃吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What if we ran?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.07,0:15:07.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}坐上你最快的船\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Took your fastest ship.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.16,0:15:08.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}带上最出色的船员\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And brightest crew.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.45,0:15:10.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}驶向天际\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And headed for the horizon.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.20,0:15:16.79,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}黄昏西行时 我们在甲板上牵着手\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Held hands on deck as we rowed west at dusk,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.87,0:15:18.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}追逐将落的太阳\N{\rEN\blur0.8}chasing the escaping sun.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.34,0:15:24.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}高墙之外 还有整个世界\N{\rEN\blur0.8}There's a world beyond these walls.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.05,0:15:30.47,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}阿伽门农会拿整个伊萨卡泄愤\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Agamemnon's vengeance will fall on all of Ithaca.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.60,0:15:37.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}答应我\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now promise me.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.15,0:15:42.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}如果我没有回来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}If I don't return
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.32,0:15:44.32,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}等忒勒马科斯成年\N{\rEN\blur0.8}by the time Telemachus comes of age,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.07,0:15:46.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}答应我\N{\rEN\blur0.8}promise me
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.66,0:15:50.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你会另嫁他人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-you'll take another husband.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.66,0:15:53.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}牺牲已经够多了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Enough sacrifices.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.29,0:15:55.04,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}爱不是牺牲\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Love's not a sacrifice.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.12,0:15:56.33,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}当然是\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Of course it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.62,0:15:59.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我不想让你牺牲\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't want you to make it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.08,0:16:01.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那可由不得你\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-It's not up to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.84,0:16:04.09,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}答应我\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Promise me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.67,0:16:06.67,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.51,0:16:12.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你先答应我会回来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Promise me you'll come back.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.85,0:16:19.14,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}要是回不来呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What if I can't?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.11,0:16:27.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那你留下的回忆也不能替我做主\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Then your memory won't be making my decisions.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.78,0:16:34.74,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}带上我的胸针\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Take my pin.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.83,0:16:36.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一直戴着\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Wear it always.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.08,0:16:38.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}雅典娜会带你回家\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Athena will bring you home.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.66,0:16:40.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我戴着未必合适\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm not sure it suits me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.71,0:16:45.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}旅人若说见过你\N{\rEN\blur0.8}When travelers claim to have seen you,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.38,0:16:47.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我就问他你穿戴什么\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'll ask what you were wearing.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.46,0:16:49.09,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这样便知道他有没有撒谎\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And I'll know if they were lying.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.43,0:16:54.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}如果真有海上民族\N{\rEN\blur0.8}If the people from the sea are real,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.72,0:16:59.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}伊萨卡如今没有能召集军队的国王\N{\rEN\blur0.8}right now, Ithaca has no king to raise an army.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.94,0:17:01.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我可以继承王位\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I could take the throne.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.65,0:17:04.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Come.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.62,0:17:17.83,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}给它上弦\N{\rEN\blur0.8}String it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.13,0:17:29.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这不公平\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's not fair.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.92,0:17:31.93,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你说过 只有他能给这张弓上弦\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You said only he could string this bow.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.01,0:17:33.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他倒乐意让别人试试\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He was happy to let others try.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.22,0:17:37.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他会把斧头一字排开\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He'd line up all the axes.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.43,0:17:40.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.42,0:18:11.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}从没有别人做到过\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No one else ever did it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.30,0:18:16.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}母亲 他们在榨干我们 逼你选一个\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Mom, they're bleeding us dry so you'll be forced to choose one of them
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.43,0:18:19.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}赶在我有资格继位之前\N{\rEN\blur0.8}before I can claim the throne myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.14,0:18:21.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那旅人说 墨涅拉俄斯几年前就回来了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The traveler told me Menelaus returned years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.60,0:18:23.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们都回来了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}They've all returned.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.10,0:18:24.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}活着的都回来了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}All who survived.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.19,0:18:27.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也许他真的死了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Maybe he is dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.15,0:18:30.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那这座王宫就该是我的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And if he is, then this is my palace.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.36,0:18:32.36,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们必须弄清楚\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We need to know.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.44,0:18:35.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我要去见墨涅拉俄斯 查明真相\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I have to go to Menelaus to find out the truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.28,0:18:36.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}忒勒马科斯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Telemachus,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.41,0:18:38.83,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这些求婚者想害你\N{\rEN\blur0.8}these suitors mean you harm.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.91,0:18:41.29,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你以为我不知道？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You think I don't know that?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.37,0:18:43.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们夜夜挑畔 就等我给他们借口\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Every night, they push me to give them the excuse they need.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.00,0:18:47.17,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可到了海上 路上呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And out there, on the sea, on the road?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.84,0:18:50.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们连借口都不用找 你就再也回不来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}They won't need an excuse. You just won't come back.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.34,0:18:54.47,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你根本不想让我自己继位\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You don't want me to claim the throne myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.47,0:19:00.31,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你只想把我困住 好继续当伊萨卡王后\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You just wanna keep me in my place so that you can stay Queen of Ithaca.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.39,0:19:03.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没有我的国王 这王后我早当够了！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I've had enough of being Queen of Ithaca without my king!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.18,0:19:05.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没有你的国王？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Without your king?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.14,0:19:07.15,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还是没有任何一位国王？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Or "a" king?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.81,0:19:11.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你以为自己能取代父亲了？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And you think you're ready to take your father's place?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.65,0:19:14.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你还是个孩子\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You're a child.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.33,0:19:27.21,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}太吵了 墨兰提俄斯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Too loud, Melanthius.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.29,0:19:29.04,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}别戴着马刺进王宫\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Don't wear your spurs in the palace.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.13,0:19:31.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你是牧牛人 又不是骑兵\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You're a cowherd, not a horseman.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.21,0:19:32.63,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你还不是个养猪的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And you're a pig farmer.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.71,0:19:35.09,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你算什么东西 敢这么跟我说话？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And who are you to talk to me like that? Hmm?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.17,0:19:38.55,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}主人临走前 让我掌管所有牧人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The servant our master left in charge of his herdsmen.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.05,0:19:42.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}主人早没了 你这老瞎子\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Our master is long gone, you blind old fool.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.77,0:19:45.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你和那条狗一样不受欢迎\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And you're about as welcome here as that dog is.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.39,0:19:47.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}阿尔戈斯！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Argus!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.11,0:19:52.15,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}阿尔戈斯！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Argus!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.48,0:19:56.15,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}阿尔戈斯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Argus.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.57,0:19:59.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}大人 他什么也没做\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Sir, he didn't do anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.24,0:20:00.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这么说 是你在发臭？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}So that stink is you?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.91,0:20:03.24,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}别欺负这条老狗\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Leave the old dog alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.33,0:20:05.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-哪一条？  -我们两个\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Which one?   -Both of us.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.46,0:20:07.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}奴才 你刚才说什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What did you say to me, slave?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.58,0:20:08.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他只是一时失言\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He just got carried away.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.67,0:20:10.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}阿尔戈斯是我父亲的猎犬\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Argus is my father's hunting dog.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.58,0:20:11.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他的猎犬？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}His hunting dog?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.01,0:20:17.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}看看这副德行\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Look at that thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.34,0:20:19.97,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}把它弄出去 我们还要吃饭\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Get it out of here. We're trying to eat.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.05,0:20:22.05,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}住手！ 没看见他疼吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Don't! Can't you see he's in pain?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.14,0:20:24.47,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好啊 那我让它解脱\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Okay. Then I'll put it out of its misery.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.97,0:20:26.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}别碰他！ 啊！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Leave him alone! Argh!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.83,0:20:44.83,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}看见没有？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Did you see?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.83,0:20:47.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们都看见了？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You all see?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.66,0:20:49.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他先动的手！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He attacked me!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.50,0:20:51.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我有权还击！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I have the right!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.25,0:20:53.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}求你！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Please!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.80,0:20:57.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}请别伤害我儿子\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Please don't hurt my son.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.59,0:21:02.47,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}冷静 波吕波斯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Easy. Easy. Polybus.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.05,0:21:05.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}小崽子一时冲动 饶了他吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The young pup lost his head. Show some mercy.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.93,0:21:08.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}来 再喝点他家的酒\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Here. Drink some more of his wine.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.93,0:21:10.31,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我来处理\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'll take care of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.90,0:21:12.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那是我父亲的猎犬\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's my father's hunting dog.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.86,0:21:15.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他活着 就为等奥德修斯回来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He's only living to see Odysseus return.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.90,0:21:16.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没事\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.98,0:21:18.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我把它放到门前的粪堆上\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'll put him on the dung heap out front
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.69,0:21:20.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好让它早点迎接主人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}so he can greet his master a little sooner.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.04,0:21:32.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那条狗就待在外面\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That dog stays out there.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.67,0:21:36.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}下次想清楚 再为一只牲口\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Next time, think twice before you offer up your life
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.34,0:21:37.67,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}搭上自己的命\N{\rEN\blur0.8}for an animal.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.14,0:21:50.14,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}欧律克勒娅\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Eurycleia.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:52.06,0:21:53.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}备好物资 送到船上\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Prepare supplies. Take them down to the ships.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.94,0:21:54.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}别告诉任何人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Tell no one.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.06,0:21:56.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}只找信得过的人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Use only people you trust.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.48,0:21:57.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你母亲会伤心欲绝\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You'll break your mother's heart.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.07,0:22:00.03,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}留下来 他们就会逼我动手\N{\rEN\blur0.8}If I stay, they'll force me to fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:00.11,0:22:01.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没人会帮我\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No one will back me.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.78,0:22:03.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我必须查清父亲的下落\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I have to find out what happened to my father.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.66,0:22:07.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}若确认奥德修斯已死 伊萨卡就会拥戴我\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Ithaca will be behind me if they know Odysseus is dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.37,0:22:08.87,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}求婚者绝不会让你得逞\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The suitors will never allow that.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:08.95,0:22:10.04,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你不可能活着回来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You will never make it back alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:10.12,0:22:14.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}告诉门托尔 黎明前到船边等我\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Tell Mentor to meet me at the ships just before dawn.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:14.08,0:22:16.79,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你母亲问起 我怎么说？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What do you want me to tell your mother?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:17.80,0:22:19.55,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}让她尽可能撑下去\N{\rEN\blur0.8}To hold out for as long as she can.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:23.22,0:22:25.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}船备好了 潮水正合适\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Ship's ready. Tide's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:25.93,0:22:28.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我说过你的眼睛透着智慧吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Have I ever told you that you have wise eyes?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:28.43,0:22:29.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}像雅典娜的眼睛？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Athena's eyes?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.89,0:22:30.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}说过一两次\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Once or twice.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:30.98,0:22:32.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你还没问我们去哪儿\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You haven't even asked me where we're going yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:33.02,0:22:34.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}去哪儿？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Where are we going?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:34.90,0:22:35.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}找我父亲\N{\rEN\blur0.8}To find my dad.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:36.60,0:22:38.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他还活着 风和海浪都在告诉我\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He's alive. I can feel it in the wind and the waves.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:39.07,0:22:40.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他就在某个地方\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He's out there somewhere,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:40.36,0:22:42.53,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}漂泊 负伤 或者迷失了方向\N{\rEN\blur0.8}wandering, injured, lost, I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:43.99,0:22:45.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}但他还活着\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But he's alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:16.85,0:23:18.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}又做梦了？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}More dreams?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:19.40,0:23:21.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}有人在溺水\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Men drowning.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:21.11,0:23:22.15,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}在里面\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:23.44,0:23:27.24,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}某个黑暗的地方\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Some dark space.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:29.58,0:23:32.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}石头上映着火光 我记不清\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Firelight on stone. I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:34.96,0:23:35.96,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你不想记起来吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Don't you wanna remember?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:36.58,0:23:39.29,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}神明为什么不把话说得明白些？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Why can't gods speak in ways we understand?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:42.00,0:23:43.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}谁听不懂雷声？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Who doesn't understand thunder?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.59,0:23:45.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}或是火焰？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Or fire?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:46.22,0:23:48.93,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}孩子的笑容 丰收的田野？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}A child's smile, a good harvest?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:49.01,0:23:51.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可你们总是隐而不现\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But you hide yourselves from us.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:52.81,0:23:53.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}看\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Look.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:54.68,0:23:56.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是谁在推动那片云？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Who's moving that cloud?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:57.06,0:23:58.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}召集那些飞鸟？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Amassing those birds?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:00.02,0:24:01.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是谁在拨动海水？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Who's moving the water?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:03.48,0:24:04.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你在跟谁说话？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Who were you talking to?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:07.70,0:24:09.11,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}雅典娜又来找我了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Athena came to me again.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:09.91,0:24:11.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}她要我想起来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}She's telling me to remember.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:13.41,0:24:14.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}要我离开\N{\rEN\blur0.8}To leave.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:14.58,0:24:15.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}为什么要走？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Why would you leave?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:16.20,0:24:18.29,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们在这里什么都有\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We have everything we need.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:18.87,0:24:20.79,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}卡吕普索 我在这里多久了？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}How long have I been here, Calypso?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:25.21,0:24:27.01,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我在别处有个家\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I have a home somewhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:28.84,0:24:29.93,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}有个人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}There's someone.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:30.55,0:24:31.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}在远方\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Out there.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:32.39,0:24:33.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你怎么知道？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}How do you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:34.06,0:24:35.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我不知道\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:37.85,0:24:38.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}但我感觉得到\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I feel.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:55.04,0:24:56.95,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们在这里 可以永远在一起\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What we have here could last forever.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:57.04,0:24:58.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}永恒属于神明\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Forever is for gods.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:58.46,0:24:59.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你是神吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Are you a god?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:02.71,0:25:03.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你想找回记忆\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You wanna remember,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:03.79,0:25:06.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可如果记忆毁掉你的幸福呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}but what if remembering destroys your happiness?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:06.38,0:25:07.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那幸福就是假的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Then it wasn't real.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:15.93,0:25:16.97,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:17.06,0:25:18.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一别再吃了 一可我喜欢\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-No more.   -But I love it.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:19.06,0:25:20.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}别再吃忘忧莲\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Stop eating the lotus.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:21.02,0:25:23.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}告诉我 你还记得什么\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Tell me what you remember.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:24.65,0:25:25.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}特洛伊之后的事\N{\rEN\blur0.8}After Troy.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:27.82,0:25:28.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}特洛伊\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Troy.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:35.20,0:25:36.49,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们赢了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We won the war.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:37.08,0:25:38.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}然后呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And then what?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:44.02,0:26:45.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}在这鬼海滩上熬了整整十年\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Ten years on this fucking beach.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:51.19,0:26:52.36,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}回家吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Let's go home.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:53.78,0:26:55.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}别忘了永远留在这里的人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Remember who we leave here.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:00.28,0:27:01.79,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}补给够吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Think we have enough provisions?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:02.58,0:27:04.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们从特洛伊拿的够多了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We've taken enough from Troy.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:05.16,0:27:06.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}多停一两站 又死不了人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Another stop or two won't kill us.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:08.42,0:27:10.55,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}起 划！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And... pull!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:11.42,0:27:13.67,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}起 划！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And... pull!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:14.59,0:27:16.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}起 划！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And... pull!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:17.80,0:27:18.97,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}起\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And...
Dialogue: 0,0:27:19.05,0:27:20.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}收桨\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Stow the oars.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:20.35,0:27:22.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}歇息！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Rest!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:22.72,0:27:25.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}收桨！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Stow the oars!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:30.36,0:27:31.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们升帆\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We'll raise the sail,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:31.61,0:27:32.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}顺着南风走\N{\rEN\blur0.8}follow the southerly winds.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:32.69,0:27:33.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是 大人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:34.74,0:27:37.11,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}阿伽门农沿熟悉的补给航线向西去了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Agamemnon's rowing west on the known provisions route.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:37.20,0:27:38.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他要养活的嘴更多\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, he's got more mouths to feed.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:39.66,0:27:40.99,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们会找到上岸的地方\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We'll find places to land.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:41.08,0:27:42.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你确定？ 这可是在冒险\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Are you sure? It's a risk.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:42.45,0:27:44.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我跟着阿伽门农够久了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I followed Agamemnon long enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:45.12,0:27:47.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}只要运气好些 风向合适\N{\rEN\blur0.8}With a little luck and the right winds,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:47.62,0:27:49.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们既能见见世面\N{\rEN\blur0.8}we'll see some of the world,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:49.46,0:27:51.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还能比阿伽门农先到家\N{\rEN\blur0.8}still be home before Agamemnon.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:54.76,0:27:55.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}稳住 伙计们！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Steady, boys!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:01.11,0:29:02.74,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}让大熊星座一直在右边\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Just keep the bear on the right.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:12.42,0:29:13.42,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}奥德修斯！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Odysseus!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:13.50,0:29:14.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}陆地！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Land!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:18.09,0:29:19.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}看见了吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}See?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:19.34,0:29:21.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你这走运的混蛋\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Lucky bastard.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:21.93,0:29:23.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}补给快耗尽了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We're down to our last supplies.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:23.60,0:29:25.14,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}召集登岸小队\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Assemble a landing party.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:25.22,0:29:27.47,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}找够三周的粮食和淡水\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Food and water. Enough for three weeks.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:27.56,0:29:28.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}要是他们不给呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What if they won't give it?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:30.81,0:29:32.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你有多想回家？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}How badly do you wanna get home?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:33.31,0:29:35.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}准备好武器！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Get your weapons ready!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:35.32,0:29:36.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一讨要 一快点！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Begging...   -Move it!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:36.57,0:29:37.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}借取\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Borrowing...
Dialogue: 0,0:29:38.48,0:29:39.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}劫掠\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Plundering.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:43.36,0:29:46.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}问他为何不迎接我们 反倒弃村而逃\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Ask him why they abandoned their village instead of welcoming us?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:53.46,0:29:55.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他说 以为我们是海上民族\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He says they thought we were the sea people.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:55.21,0:29:56.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不是\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:56.34,0:29:58.76,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们是希腊人 来来自伊萨卡\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We're Greeks. From Ithaca.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:59.67,0:30:01.42,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你或许听说了我们攻下特洛伊\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Maybe you heard of our victory at Troy.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:02.18,0:30:04.39,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们正借着南风向西航行\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We're headed west on the southerly winds.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:11.02,0:30:12.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他说 如果我们往那边去\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He says if we go that way,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:13.19,0:30:14.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}遇到的东西不会讨人喜欢\N{\rEN\blur0.8}we won't like the things we'll find.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:16.32,0:30:18.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}多年征战之后\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Affer years of war,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:19.03,0:30:22.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没人能挡住我部下的归途\N{\rEN\blur0.8}no one could stand between my men and home.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:23.82,0:30:25.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}连我也不能\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Not even me.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:26.41,0:30:28.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}后来 出了事\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Then something happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:43.97,0:30:45.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}追逐将落的太阳\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Chasing the escaping sun.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:46.55,0:30:47.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}陆地！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Land!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:49.26,0:30:50.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}陆地！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Land!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:50.68,0:30:51.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}看吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}There you go.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:55.02,0:30:56.73,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你这走运的混蛋\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Lucky bastard.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:08.82,0:31:10.49,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不 不\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No, no, no.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:10.58,0:31:12.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}羊是成群的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Sheep come in flocks.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:14.16,0:31:15.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}跟上去\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Let's follow.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:35.83,0:32:37.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这里有人住\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Someone lives here.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:38.71,0:32:39.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}对 还做奶酪\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yeah, they make cheese.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:58.73,0:32:59.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}味道不错\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Pretty good.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:02.73,0:33:03.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}数量也不少\N{\rEN\blur0.8}There's a lot of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:04.06,0:33:05.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们该走了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We should leave.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:06.03,0:33:07.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们没带东西来交换\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We brought nothing to trade with.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:08.24,0:33:09.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}宙斯的律法\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Zeus' Law.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:09.74,0:33:11.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这里的主人 未必听过宙斯的律法\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't know if whoever lives here has heard of Zeus' Law.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:11.91,0:33:13.24,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}说不定连宙斯都没听过\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Or Zeus for that matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:13.32,0:33:15.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}人人都知道宙斯的律法\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Everyone's heard of Zeus' Law.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:15.62,0:33:16.83,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}把火生起来！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Get the fire going!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:16.91,0:33:18.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}等主人回来 我们好好迎接\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We'll welcome the owner back.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:37.95,0:34:39.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}离火远点\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Get away from the fire.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:43.96,0:34:45.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}散开！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Spread out!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:18.51,0:36:19.93,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}它好像睡着了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I think it's asleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:05.26,0:37:06.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}等等\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:09.52,0:37:10.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那块石头\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The rock.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:18.28,0:37:19.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们搬不动\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We can't move the rock.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:19.36,0:37:20.74,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}会被困死在这儿\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We'd be trapped.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:29.20,0:37:30.21,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}传下去\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Spread the word.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:30.29,0:37:33.79,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}天亮后 它把羊群放出去时\N{\rEN\blur0.8}In the morning, when it lets out its flock,
Dialogue: 0,0:37:33.88,0:37:35.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们就冲向洞口\N{\rEN\blur0.8}we'll rush the entrance.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:35.42,0:37:36.55,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}养足精神\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Rest up.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:01.53,0:38:03.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}走 走 走！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Go, go, go!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:13.54,0:38:14.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}快！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Go!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:23.22,0:38:26.01,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}能不能拿东西卡住洞口？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Could we jam something in the cave mouth?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:26.09,0:38:27.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}留条缝？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Leave a gap?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:28.01,0:38:29.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也许行\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Maybe.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:30.06,0:38:31.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可用什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But what?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:31.56,0:38:32.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这根木头\N{\rEN\blur0.8}This log.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:36.36,0:38:37.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}它会发现\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It'll notice.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:39.28,0:38:41.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不过先抬起细的那头 放进火里\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But grab the thin end. Put it in the fire.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:42.78,0:38:43.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们有多少绳子？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}How much rope do we have?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:44.95,0:38:47.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-羊有多少只？  -大概二十来只\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-How big's the flock?   -Couple dozen, maybe.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:49.87,0:38:51.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们人太多了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}There's too many of us.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:51.66,0:38:54.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}它回来时 至少得有两个人逃出去\N{\rEN\blur0.8}When it comes back, two of us have to get out.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:54.16,0:38:55.67,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}逃不掉 也得死两个\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Or at least get killed.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:00.80,0:39:02.76,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}弯腰穿过羊群 冲向洞口\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Run low through the flock towards the entrance,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:02.84,0:39:03.93,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}再朝两边分头跑\N{\rEN\blur0.8}then split wide.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:04.01,0:39:06.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一这样它只能抓住一个 一对\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-So he can only grab one of 'em.   -Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:06.80,0:39:09.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}该让四个人冲出去 两人一组\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Four of us should make the run. Two and two.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:09.39,0:39:10.93,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}为什么要让更多人冒险？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Why risk more men?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:11.02,0:39:12.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}它昨晚吃了两个人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It ate two of us last night.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:12.56,0:39:14.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}睡前还会再吃两个\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He'll want another two before he sleeps.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:39.21,0:39:40.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}快走 快走！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Go, go, go!
Dialogue: 0,0:41:18.81,0:41:21.19,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一他的遗体呢？ 一怎么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What about his body? What about it?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:21.27,0:41:23.11,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就让他烂在这儿？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We just leave him here to rot?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:24.40,0:41:25.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}让那东西吃了他？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}As food for that thing?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:27.69,0:41:30.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}奥德修斯 我们要敬重死者\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We honor our dead, Odysseus.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:30.49,0:41:33.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他为助我们逃生而死 活着出去才对得起他\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He died helping us escape. We'll honor him by escaping.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:36.79,0:41:39.87,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}父亲波塞冬 他们刺瞎了我\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Father Poseidon, they blinded me.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:40.79,0:41:44.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}父亲 替我报仇 让他们偿还这痛苦\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Vengeance, Father. Vengeance for pain.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:44.42,0:41:47.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}波塞冬 替我报仇\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Poseidon, vengeance for pain.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:47.80,0:41:49.67,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}它会说话\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He can talk.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:50.34,0:41:51.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}之前怎么不说？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Why didn't it talk before?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:53.43,0:41:54.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你会跟蚂蚁说话吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Do you talk to ants?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:56.43,0:41:57.97,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}能不能跟它讲讲道理？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Should we reason with it?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:00.48,0:42:01.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}恐怕已经晚了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I think we're past that.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:13.09,0:43:14.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你在干什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What are you doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:43:15.34,0:43:17.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No!
Dialogue: 0,0:43:33.95,0:43:36.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}快走 快！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Come on. Go, go!
Dialogue: 0,0:43:36.24,0:43:38.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}快！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Go!
Dialogue: 0,0:44:06.14,0:44:07.14,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}上来！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Get in!
Dialogue: 0,0:44:09.36,0:44:10.36,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}快！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Go!
Dialogue: 0,0:44:31.67,0:44:33.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一快走 快走！ 一快走 快走！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Go, go, go! Go, go, go!
Dialogue: 0,0:44:34.42,0:44:37.09,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}快！ 快！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Go! Go!
Dialogue: 0,0:44:57.74,0:44:59.53,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你为什么非要射那一箭？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Why'd you have to fire that arrow?
Dialogue: 0,0:44:59.61,0:45:01.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那畜生杀了我们多少好战士\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We lost good soldiers to that beast.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:01.87,0:45:04.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可那畜生是波塞冬的儿子\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yeah, and that beast was the son of Poseidon.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:04.99,0:45:06.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:06.16,0:45:08.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}刺瞎它时 我们听见它喊父亲的名字\N{\rEN\blur0.8}When we put its eye out, we heard it crying his name.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:08.79,0:45:10.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那东西就是个怪物\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That thing was a monster.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:10.58,0:45:12.42,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我也听见了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I heard it too.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:12.50,0:45:14.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}所以现在连大海都与我们为敌？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}So now the sea's against us?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:14.59,0:45:16.55,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还有风\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And the wind.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:16.63,0:45:19.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}波塞冬要阻拦 我们还怎么回家？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}How are we supposed to get home with Poseidon against us?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:19.30,0:45:21.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不能事事都靠预兆和献祭\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We can't live by omens and sacrifices. y
Dialogue: 0,0:45:24.06,0:45:26.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你可知道 离开特洛伊后\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Do you know how many times I've heard you weeping,
Dialogue: 0,0:45:26.14,0:45:28.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我听过多少次你哭着向雅典娜祈祷？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}praying to Athena since we left Troy?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:28.31,0:45:29.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你就不能发发慈悲？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Couldn't you have shown some mercy?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:31.23,0:45:32.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}拿着\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Take this.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:34.82,0:45:35.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}戴上它\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Wear it.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:36.02,0:45:38.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}记住那些没能安葬的兄弟\N{\rEN\blur0.8}To remember those we couldn't bury.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:40.03,0:45:41.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}神助自助者\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The gods help those who help themselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:45.62,0:45:49.29,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}从此 每一阵逆风 每一片恶浪\N{\rEN\blur0.8}From that moment, every rough sea or headwind
Dialogue: 0,0:45:49.54,0:45:51.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}都让船员认定我们遭了诅咒\N{\rEN\blur0.8}told the crew we were cursed.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:53.54,0:45:55.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可我的船员呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But where is my crew?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:56.75,0:45:58.67,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}什么时候让我见他们？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}When will you let me see my men?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:59.67,0:46:02.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}只要聊一聊 他们就能帮我想起来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}If I could just talk to them they'd help me remember.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:02.30,0:46:03.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我有妻子吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Did I have a wife?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:03.39,0:46:04.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}孩子呢？ 也许有个儿子\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Children? Maybe a son.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:04.80,0:46:06.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我在这里多久了？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}How long have I been here?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:08.43,0:46:09.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}很久了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}A long time.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:10.06,0:46:11.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}如果我有儿子\N{\rEN\blur0.8}lf I had a son,
Dialogue: 0,0:46:13.73,0:46:15.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他现在该多大了？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}how old would he be now?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:17.28,0:46:19.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我不知道该怎么跟国王说话\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't know how to speak to a king.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:19.36,0:46:20.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没事的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You'll do fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:20.78,0:46:22.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}闭紧嘴就行\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Just keep your mouth shut.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:22.86,0:46:26.32,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}有人问起 就说我们是克里特商人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But, if anyone asks, we're traders from Crete.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:26.41,0:46:28.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}再想办法接近国王\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Then we'll figure out how to approach the king.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:38.42,0:46:39.67,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}欢迎\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Welcome.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:39.76,0:46:41.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}多谢 这里似乎正有盛大的-·\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Thank you. You seem to be having quite...
Dialogue: 0,0:46:41.88,0:46:43.09,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这边请\N{\rEN\blur0.8}This way.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:48.26,0:46:49.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}带我们去哪儿？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Where are you taking us?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:49.60,0:46:52.27,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}国王坚持亲自接见异乡人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The king insists on meeting strangers himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:13.62,0:47:14.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}坐\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Sit.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:18.17,0:47:19.17,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不是你\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Not you.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:20.55,0:47:21.55,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:23.97,0:47:25.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}请尽情享用\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Enjoy our hospitality.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:25.97,0:47:27.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}遵照宙斯的律法\N{\rEN\blur0.8}As Zeus demands.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:27.97,0:47:29.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}之后 也许你愿意说说自己的来历\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Then, perhaps, you'll tell us who you are.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:31.18,0:47:32.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们来得正是时候\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You picked the right day to arrive.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:32.89,0:47:35.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}今天是我女儿的婚宴\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Feast of my daughter's wedding.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:35.10,0:47:37.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}明天她就要离家 开始新生活\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Tomorrow she leaves to start a new life.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:38.40,0:47:40.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你不像乞写\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You don't look like a beggar.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:40.57,0:47:41.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}想必你知道我是谁\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Imagine you know who I am.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:43.78,0:47:46.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是墨涅拉俄斯 阿特柔斯之子\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm Menelaus. The son of Atreus.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:47.11,0:47:48.87,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}阿伽门农的弟弟\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Brother of Agamemnon.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:49.70,0:47:51.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}海伦的丈夫\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The husband of Helen.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:51.87,0:47:52.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你或许听说过海伦\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Perhaps you've heard of Helen.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:55.96,0:47:59.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一张面孔 令千艘战船出海\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Face that launched a thousand ships.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:01.38,0:48:03.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不过如今 顶多五百艘了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Though maybe now just 500.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:07.88,0:48:10.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}为了这张脸 多少人埋骨特洛伊\N{\rEN\blur0.8}So many left on the battlefields of Troy for that face.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:10.97,0:48:13.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是为了你兄长的野心\N{\rEN\blur0.8}For your brother's ambition.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:14.10,0:48:15.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这孩子有些眼熟\N{\rEN\blur0.8}This one looks familiar.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:17.35,0:48:18.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}埃阿斯.·-\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Ajax...
Dialogue: 0,0:48:19.06,0:48:20.11,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}帕特罗克洛斯·\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Patroclus...
Dialogue: 0,0:48:20.19,0:48:21.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}阿喀琉斯.·-\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Achilles...
Dialogue: 0,0:48:22.11,0:48:25.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我最思念的 还不是他们\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't miss them as much as one particular warrior.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:26.49,0:48:28.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那位战士 是我们中最聪明的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He was the smartest of us all.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:30.62,0:48:32.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们困在那海滩 整整十年\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Ten years we rotted on that beach.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:46.30,0:48:47.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}僵持不下\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Deadlocked.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:47.76,0:48:49.76,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}自己人斗来斗去 直到有个人-……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Fighting amongst ourselves until one man...
Dialogue: 0,0:48:53.10,0:48:54.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他想出了办法\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He found a way.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:56.18,0:48:57.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}奥德修斯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Odysseus.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:58.52,0:48:59.73,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}听过木马的故事吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You hear the story of the horse?
Dialogue: 0,0:49:03.48,0:49:04.73,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可听过木马里面的人怎么说？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But did you hear it from the inside?
Dialogue: 0,0:49:09.61,0:49:10.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们在里面待了好几天\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We were in there for days.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:12.24,0:49:14.83,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}船还没起航 我们就挤了进去\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We squeezed inside before the ship set sail.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:16.29,0:49:18.75,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}奥德修斯不让任何人知道我们藏在里面\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Odysseus, he knew that no one could know that we were inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:18.83,0:49:21.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}连我们留下的士兵西农都不知道\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Not even Sinon, the soldier we left behind.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:27.09,0:49:29.97,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}头两次涨潮 同伴就在我们眼前溺死\N{\rEN\blur0.8}First two tides, our men drowned right in front of us.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:35.72,0:49:38.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们躺在屎尿中 一声不\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We lay silent. In our piss and shit.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:06.84,0:50:08.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一份礼物\N{\rEN\blur0.8}A gift.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:08.63,0:50:10.01,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}献给雅典娜的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}For Athena.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:12.34,0:50:13.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们信奉同样的神\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Common gods.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:14.30,0:50:15.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}要尊重他们的供奉\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Respect their offering.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:37.39,0:51:39.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}该把你烧了！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You should be burned!
Dialogue: 0,0:51:39.60,0:51:41.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}烧掉！ 烧掉！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Burn it! Burn it!
Dialogue: 0,0:52:03.91,0:52:05.29,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这是献给雅典娜的供品！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's an offering for Athena!
Dialogue: 0,0:52:14.38,0:52:16.63,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这是献给雅典娜的供品！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's an offering for Athena!
Dialogue: 0,0:54:52.62,0:54:53.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}城门！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The gates!
Dialogue: 0,0:54:55.54,0:54:57.63,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他特意等到一个没有月亮的夜晚\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He knew fo wait for a moonless night
Dialogue: 0,0:54:57.71,0:54:59.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}才在特洛伊平原行动\N{\rEN\blur0.8}on the plains of Troy.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:06.01,0:55:07.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}快！ 快！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Go! Go!
Dialogue: 0,0:55:12.60,0:55:14.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}有人攻城！ 快快去城门！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}City's under attack! Get to the gates!
Dialogue: 0,0:55:15.40,0:55:16.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}去城门！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}To the gates!
Dialogue: 0,0:55:35.62,0:55:36.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}快走！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Go, go!
Dialogue: 0,0:55:37.88,0:55:39.67,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}有人攻城！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The city's under attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:56:51.41,0:56:53.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一快！ 一快走 快走！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Come on! Go, go!
Dialogue: 0,0:57:26.53,0:57:28.24,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}后面的事 你想必知道了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I think you know the rest.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:28.32,0:57:29.32,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我的讲述让你动容了？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You moved by my telling it?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:29.40,0:57:31.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你该听听吟游诗人怎么唱\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You should hear the bards sing it.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:31.66,0:57:32.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我听过\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I have.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:36.20,0:57:37.75,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可他们没跟你们亲历这一切\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But they weren't there with all of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:37.83,0:57:39.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没跟你父亲一起\N{\rEN\blur0.8}With your father.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:39.66,0:57:41.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}奥德修斯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Odysseus.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:43.75,0:57:45.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你真像他\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You're so like him.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:45.88,0:57:47.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你最后一次见他是什么时候？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}When did you last see him?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:47.55,0:57:48.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}在特洛伊\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Troy.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:49.55,0:57:51.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}神明赐予我们正义的胜利……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The gods granted us a righteous victory...
Dialogue: 0,0:57:51.80,0:57:52.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}正义\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Righteous.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:53.80,0:57:57.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}神明让我们赢得正义之战 却没保佑归途\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The gods granted our righteous victory but did not bless our voyages.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:58.77,0:58:00.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我花了好几年才回到家\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Took me years to get home.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:00.89,0:58:01.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可他没有回来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But he didn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:01.98,0:58:03.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}有人回来了 却后悔回来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Some did and wished they hadn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:03.60,0:58:05.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}告诉他\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Tell him.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:05.94,0:58:08.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一讲讲你兄长的事 一别说了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Tell him about your brother. No.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:08.69,0:58:10.03,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}讲讲神明给他的结局\N{\rEN\blur0.8}About the fate that the gods bestowed on him
Dialogue: 0,0:58:10.11,0:58:11.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}在你们那场正义之战后\N{\rEN\blur0.8}after your righteous struggle.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:11.70,0:58:13.36,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一别说了 一说说他凯旋时受到的礼遇\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-No.   -About his hero's welcome.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:13.45,0:58:14.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一别说了 一讲讲阿伽门农\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-No.   -About how Agamemnon
Dialogue: 0,0:58:14.87,0:58:16.83,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一比我们早几年到家 一别说了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-made it home years before us. No.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:16.91,0:58:19.04,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}告诉他 你的王嫂如何迎接丈夫\N{\rEN\blur0.8}7ell him how he was welcomed by his queen,
Dialogue: 0,0:58:19.12,0:58:20.87,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我的李生姐妹 克吕泰涅斯特拉\N{\rEN\blur0.8}my twin sister Clytemnestra.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:20.96,0:58:22.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一别说了 一说说她如何-·\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Wo. Wo. 7ell him how she...
Dialogue: 0,0:58:22.46,0:58:24.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}够了！ 他不想听我兄长的事！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No! He does not want to hear about my brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:58:28.13,0:58:29.42,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他想打听自己的父亲\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He wants news of his father.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:30.59,0:58:32.97,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}离开特洛伊后 我再没他的消息\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I know nothing of Odysseus since Troy.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:33.05,0:58:34.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一点都没有？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Nothing?
Dialogue: 0,0:58:35.47,0:58:37.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你的部下没人知道？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Not from any of your men?
Dialogue: 0,0:58:37.93,0:58:40.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}阿伽门农的部下 商人或旅人都没说过？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Or Agamemnon's, or traders, or travelers that told you something?
Dialogue: 0,0:58:40.52,0:58:43.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你来这儿就是为了听传言 听闲话？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Ah, did you come here for rumors? Is that what you're interested in? Gossip?
Dialogue: 0,0:58:44.35,0:58:45.73,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那可来对地方了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, you're in the right place.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:45.81,0:58:48.73,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}谁想编段奥德修斯的故事？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Anyone wanna spin a story about Odysseus?
Dialogue: 0,0:58:49.23,0:58:52.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}有人说他富甲一方 有人说他穷困潦倒\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Some say he's rich or some say poor.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:53.11,0:58:55.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}有人说他死了 有人说他身陷图图\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Some say he perished. Some say he's in prison.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:55.66,0:58:57.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你怎么说？  -身陷图圈？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-What say you?   -In prison?
Dialogue: 0,0:59:00.50,0:59:01.83,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}什么样的牢狱\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What kind of prison
Dialogue: 0,0:59:02.75,0:59:04.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}能困住他那样的人？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}could hold a man like that?
Dialogue: 0,0:59:05.58,0:59:07.75,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}先说你记得的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Tell me what you do remember.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:07.84,0:59:08.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}其他的会慢慢想起来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The rest will come.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:10.17,0:59:13.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}船员越来越确信 我冒犯了波塞冬\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The men became more and more convinced that I'd offended Poseidon.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:34.40,0:59:36.49,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一准备！ 一准备！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Ready! Ready!
Dialogue: 0,0:59:37.82,0:59:39.24,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}划！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Pull!
Dialogue: 0,0:59:39.83,0:59:42.83,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}起 划！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And... pull!
Dialogue: 0,0:59:44.29,0:59:46.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}起 划！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-And... pull!
Dialogue: 0,0:59:57.76,0:59:59.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}划！ 起\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Pull! And...
Dialogue: 0,0:59:59.76,1:00:01.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}暴风雨接而至\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We were hit by storm after storm.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:01.72,1:00:03.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一次次把我们推离航线\N{\rEN\blur0.8}All pushing us off course.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:03.98,1:00:05.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}直到我们彻底迷失方向\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Until we were truly lost.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:09.69,1:00:14.53,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}起 划！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-And... pull!   -And... pull!
Dialogue: 0,1:00:16.99,1:00:17.99,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}划！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Pull!
Dialogue: 0,1:00:18.86,1:00:24.96,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}起 划！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-And... pull! And... pull!
Dialogue: 0,1:00:58.40,1:00:59.49,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你好\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Hello.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:01.41,1:01:02.45,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们没有恶意\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We're here in peace.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:05.20,1:01:06.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}只想找点食物\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We just need some food.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:12.84,1:01:14.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们需要食物\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We need food.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:15.84,1:01:17.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-听得懂吗？  -只是个孩子\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Can you understand that?   -It's just a child.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:20.51,1:01:23.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}孩子都这么大 父母得多大？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}If that's a child, what about its parents?
Dialogue: 0,1:01:25.26,1:01:27.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}嘿 嘘 没事的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Hey. Shh! It's okay.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:27.85,1:01:30.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}别 别\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-No, no, no.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:49.04,1:01:51.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}快跑！ 快！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Go! Go!
Dialogue: 0,1:01:51.17,1:01:53.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}回船上！ 快！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Back to the ship! Go!
Dialogue: 0,1:02:08.06,1:02:09.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}快走 快！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Go, go. Go.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:18.19,1:02:20.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}撤退！ 快！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Fall back! Fall back! Go! Go!
Dialogue: 0,1:03:30.18,1:03:31.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}跑！ 快点！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Run! Faster!
Dialogue: 0,1:03:41.07,1:03:43.36,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}拿我的弓来！ 我的弓！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Get my bow! My bow!
Dialogue: 0,1:03:47.74,1:03:48.87,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}走！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Let's go!
Dialogue: 0,1:03:58.29,1:04:00.21,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}快走！ 快！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Let's go! Come on!
Dialogue: 0,1:04:00.30,1:04:01.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}起 划！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And... pull!
Dialogue: 0,1:04:01.80,1:04:03.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}等等！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Wait!
Dialogue: 0,1:04:03.84,1:04:05.42,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}起 划！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And... pull!
Dialogue: 0,1:04:05.51,1:04:06.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}等等！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Wait!
Dialogue: 0,1:04:06.93,1:04:08.39,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}起 划！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And... pull!
Dialogue: 0,1:04:08.97,1:04:11.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}起 划！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And... pull!
Dialogue: 0,1:04:11.97,1:04:13.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}起 划！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And... pull!
Dialogue: 0,1:04:14.06,1:04:15.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}快！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Go!
Dialogue: 0,1:04:15.18,1:04:17.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}等等！ 起 划！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Wait! And... pull!
Dialogue: 0,1:04:18.73,1:04:19.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}等等！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Wait!
Dialogue: 0,1:04:30.58,1:04:31.99,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}用桨撑开！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Push the oars!
Dialogue: 0,1:04:37.83,1:04:41.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}快！ 把这破船撑出去！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}All right! Move this bastard!
Dialogue: 0,1:05:34.72,1:05:35.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}向左舷转\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Turn to port.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:35.89,1:05:37.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}沿着海岸走\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Follow the coast.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:37.56,1:05:39.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们也有船怎么办？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What if they have ships?
Dialogue: 0,1:05:39.14,1:05:41.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们得尽快远离这里\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We need to get as far away as possible.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:45.98,1:05:48.24,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}补给不够 不能贸然横渡大海\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We don't have supplies for a blind crossing.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:48.94,1:05:50.74,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们已迷失方向\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We've lost our way.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:50.82,1:05:53.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}得找食物 也得辨明方位\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We need to find food and get our bearings.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:56.54,1:05:57.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}向左舷转\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Turn to port.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:24.27,1:06:27.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那里！ 有烟！ 看！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}There! Smoke! There!
Dialogue: 0,1:06:27.36,1:06:30.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}驶过去 在海滩附近找地方下锚！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Go past, we'll find anchorage at the beach!
Dialogue: 0,1:06:37.33,1:06:38.79,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}收桨！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oars up!
Dialogue: 0,1:06:42.50,1:06:44.63,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}召集登岸小队\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Form a landing party.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:46.42,1:06:48.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}明天再去\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Tomorrow.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:50.30,1:06:51.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}明天\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Tomorrow.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:01.89,1:07:03.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}留个人看守小艇\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Leave someone with the tenders.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:04.56,1:07:06.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们觉得你该留下\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We think you should stay.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:08.65,1:07:10.32,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我们？  -所有人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-"We'"?   -All of us.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:10.98,1:07:12.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还活着的所有人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Still alive.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:23.00,1:07:24.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们要哗变？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Is this a mutiny?
Dialogue: 0,1:07:24.46,1:07:25.83,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那就看你了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's up to you.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:29.96,1:07:30.96,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}把弓给我\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Give me your bow.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:31.05,1:07:32.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}今晚我会让大家吃上东西\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'll make sure we eat tonight.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:33.47,1:07:34.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不管你们找到了什么\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No matter what you find.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:21.45,1:09:23.87,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不 不！ 没事的！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No, no! It's okay! It's okay!
Dialogue: 0,1:09:27.83,1:09:28.96,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-求你别伤害我！  -没事的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Please don't hurt me!   -It's okay.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:29.04,1:09:30.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-别怕！ 没事的！  -不！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-You're okay! It's all right!   -No!
Dialogue: 0,1:09:30.46,1:09:31.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没人会伤害你！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No one's gonna hurt you!
Dialogue: 0,1:09:31.54,1:09:33.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}只要我乖乖听话？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}If I do what you want.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:33.34,1:09:35.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没人会伤害你\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No one is going to hurt you.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:39.38,1:09:41.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我叫欧律洛科斯 你叫什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}My name's Eurylochus. What's your name?
Dialogue: 0,1:09:41.39,1:09:42.47,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}喀耳刻\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Circe.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:42.55,1:09:45.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}喀耳刻 我们急需食物\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Circe, we need food. Badly.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:46.56,1:09:47.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我有食物\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I have food.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:49.52,1:09:50.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}有很多\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Lots of food.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:12.33,1:10:13.42,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}来 我帮你\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Here, let me.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:16.55,1:10:18.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}武器和盔甲\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Your weapons, your armor,
Dialogue: 0,1:10:19.92,1:10:21.01,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}放到后面去\N{\rEN\blur0.8}put it out the back.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:55.21,1:10:57.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}嗯……嗯·\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Mmm... Mmm...
Dialogue: 0,1:11:04.18,1:11:05.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}喜欢我的肉吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You like my meat?
Dialogue: 0,1:11:06.39,1:11:08.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你怎么会有这么多？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Why... do you have so much?
Dialogue: 0,1:11:09.72,1:11:12.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}谁知道什么时候会有客人来呢\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You never know when strangers will come.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:22.70,1:11:23.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}男人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Men.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:26.16,1:11:27.87,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}带着他们的欲望\N{\rEN\blur0.8}With their appetites.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:29.45,1:11:31.33,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}再多也填不满\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Too much is never enough.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:47.24,1:12:48.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}欧律洛科斯！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Eurylochus!
Dialogue: 0,1:13:14.43,1:13:15.73,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们还没回来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}They haven't come back yet.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:15.81,1:13:16.93,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一个都没回？ 一没有\N{\rEN\blur0.8}None of them? No.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:17.02,1:13:18.19,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}把匕首给我\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Give me your dagger.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:21.90,1:13:22.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}守着船！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Stay with the boat!
Dialogue: 0,1:14:04.40,1:14:05.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}怎么不直接过来？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Why don't you just come here?
Dialogue: 0,1:14:14.24,1:14:15.99,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你从海上来？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Do you come from the sea?
Dialogue: 0,1:14:17.83,1:14:19.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就你一个人？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Are you alone?
Dialogue: 0,1:14:24.25,1:14:26.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我的猪很喜欢你\N{\rEN\blur0.8}My pigs have taken a liking to you.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:27.25,1:14:28.63,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}饿了吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Are you hungry?
Dialogue: 0,1:14:30.76,1:14:32.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}把武器放在门口\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Leave your weapons at the door.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:32.68,1:14:35.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}依宙斯的律法 好好享用吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Enjoy the hospitality of Zeus.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:36.56,1:14:39.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}挑头猪吧 杀了当晚餐\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Grab a hog. You can slaughter it for your dinner.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:04.58,1:15:07.21,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不管你是谁 显然不是个农夫\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Whoever you are, you're clearly not a farmer.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:07.29,1:15:08.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}给\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Here.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:12.13,1:15:13.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}炖肉闻起来不错\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That stew smells good.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:17.22,1:15:18.97,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}只够我们两个吃\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-That's enough for just us.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:20.02,1:15:21.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}谁说这里只有我们两个？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Who says it's just us?
Dialogue: 0,1:15:23.10,1:15:24.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还有谁？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Who else is here?
Dialogue: 0,1:15:25.06,1:15:27.19,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是啊 还有谁呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Who indeed?
Dialogue: 0,1:15:39.28,1:15:40.74,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你说自己独自一人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You say you're all alone.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:41.58,1:15:44.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可没人会独自来这里\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-But no one comes here alone.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:44.16,1:15:45.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No?
Dialogue: 0,1:15:45.62,1:15:48.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这里只有坐船才能到\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You can only reach this spot by sea.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:48.67,1:15:51.09,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那你的同船伙伴呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}So where are your shipmates?
Dialogue: 0,1:15:51.96,1:15:53.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我在找他们\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm looking for them.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:54.30,1:15:55.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}有没有人来过这里？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Anyone happen to come this way?
Dialogue: 0,1:15:59.10,1:16:00.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可你准备了这么多食物？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But you prepared all this food?
Dialogue: 0,1:16:00.77,1:16:03.14,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你在盘问我？ 就凭你？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You're questioning me? You?
Dialogue: 0,1:16:05.27,1:16:07.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一个显然饿坏了的旅人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}A traveler who's clearly starving,
Dialogue: 0,1:16:07.52,1:16:09.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}却对面前的食物一口不动\N{\rEN\blur0.8}yet hasn't touched the food in front of him.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:09.86,1:16:13.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}自称水手 却穿着勇士的盔甲\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Claims to be a sailor, yet wears a great warrior's armor.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:14.40,1:16:16.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还违背宙斯的律法\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And who breaks Zeus' Law
Dialogue: 0,1:16:16.78,1:16:19.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}把匕首带进女主人的家\N{\rEN\blur0.8}by bringing a dagger into his hostess' house.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:19.78,1:16:21.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你的眼睛很锐利\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You have sharp eyes.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:21.16,1:16:23.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是神明赐予的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Sharpened by the gods.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:23.75,1:16:25.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们让你洞察一切？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Do they grant you insights?
Dialogue: 0,1:16:25.75,1:16:27.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}洞察真相\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Truths.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:28.29,1:16:29.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}有时如此\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Sometimes.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:29.79,1:16:31.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}能告诉你我的部下在哪儿吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Would they tell you where I could find my men?
Dialogue: 0,1:16:32.80,1:16:33.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你的部下？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Your men?
Dialogue: 0,1:16:34.01,1:16:35.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没错\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's right.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:35.76,1:16:37.09,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}能\N{\rEN\blur0.8}They would.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:37.18,1:16:38.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那你愿意告诉我吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And would you tell me?
Dialogue: 0,1:16:38.93,1:16:40.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也许\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Perhaps.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:41.93,1:16:43.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}把匕首给我\N{\rEN\blur0.8}If you give me your dagger.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:52.15,1:16:55.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可我为何要帮一个拒绝款待的骗子？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But why would I help a liar who refuses my hospitality?
Dialogue: 0,1:17:06.29,1:17:09.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你的部下来过 现在不在了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Your men were here earlier, and now they're not.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:15.80,1:17:16.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们走了？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}They moved on?
Dialogue: 0,1:17:17.42,1:17:18.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}对\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yes.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:21.30,1:17:22.93,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}却留下了戒指？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Leaving their rings?
Dialogue: 0,1:17:30.60,1:17:31.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}换作我就不会动\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I wouldn't.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:33.40,1:17:34.27,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}别动\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Don't.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:34.36,1:17:36.11,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我不知道这只乌鸦对你有何意义\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't know who this crow is to you,
Dialogue: 0,1:17:36.19,1:17:39.24,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}但你不放下刀 我就掐死它看看\N{\rEN\blur0.8}but if you don't put that knife down, I will throttle it to find out.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:39.32,1:17:40.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}别伤害她\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Don't hurt her.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:40.70,1:17:41.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}家人？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Family?
Dialogue: 0,1:17:43.78,1:17:45.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}母亲？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Mother?
Dialogue: 0,1:17:47.33,1:17:48.33,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你的姐妹\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Your sister.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:52.00,1:17:54.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你把她变成这样 也把我的人变成了猪\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You did this to her like you turned my men into pigs.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:54.80,1:17:56.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我没把你的部下变成任何东西\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I didn't turn your men into anything.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:57.30,1:18:00.01,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}看看他们 这就是他们的本性！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Look at them. This is who they are. Look at them!
Dialogue: 0,1:18:00.59,1:18:02.97,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}卑劣 肮脏\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Base. Disgusting.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:03.05,1:18:05.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你在战场上 看重的正是这种兽性\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Primal urges that you value in battle.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:05.68,1:18:08.27,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们为你四处奸淫掳掠\N{\rEN\blur0.8}They've raped and pillaged across the world for you.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:08.35,1:18:10.14,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你以为那违背了他们的本性？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And you think that's against their nature?
Dialogue: 0,1:18:10.23,1:18:12.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}以为他们只是奉命行事？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You think they only did that because you ordered them to?
Dialogue: 0,1:18:12.56,1:18:16.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}真正的统帅 会把部下的残暴视为纪律\N{\rEN\blur0.8}A true commander thinks his men's savagery is actually discipline.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:17.32,1:18:19.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可你似乎没那么糊涂\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But you don't seem that deluded.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:19.49,1:18:21.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你却把他们派到我这里\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But you sent them to me here.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:21.36,1:18:22.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}来找独居的我\N{\rEN\blur0.8}On my own.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:22.99,1:18:26.87,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一群肮脏的士兵 饥肠 血气方刚！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}A gang of filthy soldiers with empty bellies and hot blood!
Dialogue: 0,1:18:28.16,1:18:31.79,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你以为他们会尊重我 尊重我的家？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You thought they'd respect me in my home?
Dialogue: 0,1:18:32.54,1:18:33.79,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}看看他们！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Look at them!
Dialogue: 0,1:18:33.88,1:18:34.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}认清你的部下\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Know your own men.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:36.71,1:18:37.96,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们伤害你了吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Did they hurt you?
Dialogue: 0,1:18:38.05,1:18:39.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们本来会的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}They would've.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:39.96,1:18:41.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们只是想回家\N{\rEN\blur0.8}They just wanna go home.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:45.10,1:18:46.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}放他们走吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Let them.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:12.41,1:19:13.83,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}回来吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Come back.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:14.88,1:19:16.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}回来吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Come back.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:17.17,1:19:18.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}回来吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Come back.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:18.67,1:19:20.67,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}重新披上你们的伪装\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Back into your disguises.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:24.88,1:19:26.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}回来吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Come back.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:26.43,1:19:28.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}重新披上你们的伪装\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Back into your disguises.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:28.89,1:19:30.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}回来吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Come back.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:30.68,1:19:32.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}重新披上你们的伪装\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Back into your disguises.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:32.98,1:19:35.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}回来吧 回来吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Come back. Come back.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:36.56,1:19:37.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}回来吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Come back.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:37.86,1:19:40.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}重新披上你们的伪装\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Back into your disguises.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:40.48,1:19:42.11,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}回来吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Come back.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:45.78,1:19:47.24,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}奥德修斯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Odysseus.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:47.32,1:19:48.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}回船上！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Back to the ship!
Dialogue: 0,1:19:48.87,1:19:50.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}能带多少食物就带多少\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Take all the food you can carry.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:50.66,1:19:52.29,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}肉留下\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Leave the meat.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:52.37,1:19:54.83,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你不能饶她 她是巫女\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You're not gonna let her live. She's a witch.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:54.92,1:19:56.42,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是谁赐她力量？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Who gave her powers?
Dialogue: 0,1:19:56.50,1:19:58.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们的神\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Your gods.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:58.17,1:20:00.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}去溪边装满水罐和皮囊\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Fill the jugs and skins at the stream.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:00.21,1:20:01.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}天亮起航\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Be ready to sail at dawn.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:07.43,1:20:09.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}为什么让她一直保持这样？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Why leave her like this?
Dialogue: 0,1:20:09.68,1:20:11.31,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这样我们相处得更好\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We get on better this way.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:12.77,1:20:14.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}若有冒犯 请原谅\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm sorry if we offended you.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:15.69,1:20:17.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没有你的帮助 我们回不了家\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We can't get back without your help.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:17.98,1:20:20.11,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们得找到通往商路的航线\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We need to know the way to the trade routes.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:20.19,1:20:21.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们已经完全迷失了方向\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You're too lost.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:21.98,1:20:23.03,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}什么意思？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,1:20:24.61,1:20:27.36,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}只有盲先知忒瑞西阿斯能指引你回家\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Only blind Tiresias can tell you how to go home.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:27.45,1:20:28.45,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}忒瑞西阿斯？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Tiresias?
Dialogue: 0,1:20:28.53,1:20:30.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他在冥府\N{\rEN\blur0.8}In Hades.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:30.20,1:20:33.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没人能驶进冥府 还活着回来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Nobody sails into Hell. And comes back.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:33.29,1:20:34.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你能\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You will.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:35.91,1:20:37.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}向北驶入暮色\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Head north. Into the twilight.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:43.50,1:20:45.42,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}再转入内陆\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Then head inland.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:45.51,1:20:48.55,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}直到火河与冰河交汇\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Until the river of fire meets a river of ice.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:39.02,1:21:40.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}在那里挖一道沟\N{\rEN\blur0.8}There you must dig a trench.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:43.73,1:21:45.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}用祭牲的鲜血将它灌满\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And fill it with the blood of sacrifice.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:06.13,1:22:07.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}召来亡者\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Gather the dead.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:08.76,1:22:10.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}问出归家的路\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And learn how you go home.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:12.47,1:22:13.76,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是你\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:14.80,1:22:16.27,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不是你的部下\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Not your men.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:16.89,1:22:18.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你诅咒了他们？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You cursed them?
Dialogue: 0,1:22:18.60,1:22:19.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不是诅咒\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Not a curse.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:21.02,1:22:22.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是事实\N{\rEN\blur0.8}A truth.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:23.10,1:22:25.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你的部下不愿你违抗神明\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Your men don't want you to defy the gods.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:27.48,1:22:29.74,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可神明说 只有你能回家\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But the gods say only you make it home.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:30.82,1:22:32.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那我就违抗神明\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Then I defy the gods.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:14.07,1:23:15.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}西农\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Sinon.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:15.78,1:23:16.95,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是奥德修斯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's Odysseus.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:21.66,1:23:22.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}西农\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Sinon.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:23.83,1:23:24.83,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是奥德修斯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's Odysseus.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:27.63,1:23:29.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}让他喝吧 奥德修斯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Let him drink, Odysseus.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:30.17,1:23:32.01,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}然后你就能听到他的陈述\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Then you'll hear his testament.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:46.48,1:23:47.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}奥德修斯？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Odysseus?
Dialogue: 0,1:23:47.73,1:23:48.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是我\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yes.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:48.98,1:23:51.03,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你骗了所有人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You lied to everyone.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:54.90,1:23:56.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}非要连我也骗吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Did you have to lie to me?
Dialogue: 0,1:23:57.74,1:23:59.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我需要你信以为真\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I needed you to believe.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:01.37,1:24:03.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你为什么非要自愿来？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Why did you have to volunteer?
Dialogue: 0,1:24:03.46,1:24:05.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你不记得我是怎么来的？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Don't you remember how I came here?
Dialogue: 0,1:24:05.33,1:24:08.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我求着顶替安提诺俄斯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I begged to take Antinous' place.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:08.34,1:24:09.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他被抽中了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Hed been called.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:10.63,1:24:13.97,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他答应给你家人钱 让你替他去\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He offered money for your family if you'd take his place.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:14.55,1:24:16.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}如果特洛伊人不让我活\N{\rEN\blur0.8}If the Trojans don't let me live,
Dialogue: 0,1:24:18.97,1:24:20.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}如果我回不了家\N{\rEN\blur0.8}if I never make it home,
Dialogue: 0,1:24:20.51,1:24:22.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}把这个带给我父亲\N{\rEN\blur0.8}take this back to my father.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:23.85,1:24:25.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}告诉他我做过的一切\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Tell him everything I did.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:28.52,1:24:30.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}奥德修斯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Odysseus.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:31.36,1:24:33.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不妨再添点光彩\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Feel free to add some stuff.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:37.03,1:24:39.45,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你信不过我 不肯说实话？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You didn't trust me with the truth?
Dialogue: 0,1:24:41.16,1:24:43.29,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你知道我肯为你死\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You knew I'd die for you.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:43.37,1:24:46.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}人之将死 其言也真 我必须让你相信\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Dying men tell the truth. I needed you to believe.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:46.33,1:24:49.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我为你的谎言死在了海滩上\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I died for your lie on that beach.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:49.88,1:24:51.96,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我知道 我就在那里\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I know. I was there with you.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:52.67,1:24:55.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我听着你用最后一口气重复谎言\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I heard you repeat the lie with your dying breath.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:55.67,1:24:57.01,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}为我们赢得战争\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Winning us the war.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:57.09,1:24:58.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我就在你身旁 尺之遥\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I was right there. Inches from you.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:58.88,1:24:59.93,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}闻着你的血腥味\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Smelling your blood.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:00.01,1:25:02.01,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这又能给我什么安慰？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What comfort could that give me?
Dialogue: 0,1:25:03.43,1:25:07.39,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}直到死者告诉我 才知道你藏在木马里\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Not knowing you were inside that horse until the dead told me.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:08.40,1:25:09.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哪些死者？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Which dead?
Dialogue: 0,1:25:09.69,1:25:13.32,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这片海岸上 多的是为你征战的老兵\N{\rEN\blur0.8}A lot of veterans of your campaigns walk these shores.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:15.53,1:25:20.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}亡者聚在一起哀叹生者 迎接新魂\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The dead meet to lament the living and greet the newly dead.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:20.87,1:25:23.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我父亲是第一个找到我的亡魂\N{\rEN\blur0.8}My father was the first shade to find me.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:23.99,1:25:25.45,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}来安慰你\N{\rEN\blur0.8}To comfort you.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:25.54,1:25:27.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}亡魂不会安慰人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Shades don't comfort.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:27.71,1:25:30.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们只想打听那些亏欠他们的生者\N{\rEN\blur0.8}They want word of the living who wronged them.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:31.75,1:25:34.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我父亲穷困而死\N{\rEN\blur0.8}My father had died in poverty,
Dialogue: 0,1:25:34.34,1:25:39.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}孤身一人 向安提诺俄斯之流乞食\N{\rEN\blur0.8}alone, begging for scraps from people like Antinous.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:39.38,1:25:41.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}安提诺俄斯骗了你？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Antinous cheated you?
Dialogue: 0,1:25:41.80,1:25:43.93,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他也一定在骗你\N{\rEN\blur0.8}As he's no doubt cheating you.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:44.01,1:25:44.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}怎么骗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}How?
Dialogue: 0,1:25:44.93,1:25:47.39,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}伊萨卡如今是谁在照顾你的妻儿？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Who's in Ithaca looking after your wife and son?
Dialogue: 0,1:25:47.48,1:25:49.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我不担心妻子\N{\rEN\blur0.8}My wife is of no concern.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:51.15,1:25:53.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}问问阿伽门农 归家是什么滋味\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Talk to Agamemnon about homecomings.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:54.27,1:25:55.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}等等 阿伽门农在这里？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Wait. Agamemnon's here?
Dialogue: 0,1:25:59.07,1:26:01.36,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你在特洛伊体面地安葬了我\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You buried me at Troy with respect.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:01.45,1:26:02.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}谢谢\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:03.28,1:26:05.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可也想想那些没能入土的同伴\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But spare a thought for those you didn't.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:05.70,1:26:07.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不是每次都办得到\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's not always possible.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:08.25,1:26:11.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}回家以后 带一条船\N{\rEN\blur0.8}When you get home, take a ship.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:11.46,1:26:14.67,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}驶向未知的西方 直直到找到陆地\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Head into the unknown west till you find land.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:14.75,1:26:16.76,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}在那里献祭\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And there, give sacrifice
Dialogue: 0,1:26:16.84,1:26:18.96,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}祭奠你的部下\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and honor your men.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:20.55,1:26:22.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那支签还留着吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Do you still have the lot?
Dialogue: 0,1:26:25.85,1:26:27.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}当然\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Of course.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:27.60,1:26:28.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}如果你能回家\N{\rEN\blur0.8}If you make it home,
Dialogue: 0,1:26:28.68,1:26:30.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}把安提诺俄斯的耻辱还给他\N{\rEN\blur0.8}give Antinous back his shame.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:30.85,1:26:31.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我会的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I will.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:43.36,1:26:44.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}陛下\N{\rEN\blur0.8}My lord.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:56.00,1:26:57.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}奥德修斯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Odysseus.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:58.09,1:26:59.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你怎么会在这里？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}How are you here?
Dialogue: 0,1:26:59.84,1:27:01.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们赢了战争 你也踏上了归途\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We won the war. You headed for home.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:02.38,1:27:05.97,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}奥德修斯 我下最出色的将军\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Odysseus, the most brilliant of all my generals.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:07.26,1:27:08.93,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你绝不会像我一样落入圈套\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You would never be snared as I was.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:09.02,1:27:10.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你也像我们一样 在海上漂流？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Were you cast adrift? Like us?
Dialogue: 0,1:27:11.39,1:27:12.39,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:12.48,1:27:14.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我的不幸 正是回到了家\N{\rEN\blur0.8}My misfortune was to make it home.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:15.65,1:27:17.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}受到美丽妻子的迎接\N{\rEN\blur0.8}To be welcomed by my beautiful wife.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:23.99,1:27:25.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}沐浴\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Bathed.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:27.62,1:27:28.95,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}涂油\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Anointed.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:31.08,1:27:32.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}卸下戒备\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Made soft.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:33.16,1:27:34.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}才得到最惨痛的教训\N{\rEN\blur0.8}To learn the hardest lesson.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:35.71,1:27:38.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}多年前 我已在她心里种下怨毒\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That I'd left a poison in her heart years before.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:41.21,1:27:42.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}而她心中的爱 早已给了别人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Good part of her heart had gone to another.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:45.89,1:27:48.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不！ 不！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No! No.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:49.22,1:27:51.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}她和情夫密谋多年 要杀死我\N{\rEN\blur0.8}She and her lover had plotted my murder for years.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:53.31,1:27:54.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}奥德修斯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Odysseus.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:55.48,1:27:56.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我在\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yes.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:56.77,1:28:00.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我儿俄瑞斯忒斯 为我报仇了吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}My son Orestes, did he avenge me?
Dialogue: 0,1:28:00.36,1:28:01.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}陛下 我怎会知道？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}My lord, how could I know?
Dialogue: 0,1:28:02.78,1:28:04.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我还在设法回家\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm still trying to get home.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:05.53,1:28:07.03,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}别重蹈我的覆辙\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Don't make my mistake.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:08.16,1:28:11.29,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}别大摇大摆进家门 盼着鲜花和赞美\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Don't walk in the front door expecting garlands and praise.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:12.00,1:28:13.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}乔装回去\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Come in disguise.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:14.16,1:28:15.21,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}耐心些\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Take your time.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:16.08,1:28:17.21,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}看清形势\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Assess.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:24.01,1:28:25.47,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}明白了吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Do you see?
Dialogue: 0,1:28:27.30,1:28:28.76,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我知道该怎么做\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I know what I have to do.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:28.84,1:28:30.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你只知道一部分\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Some of what you have to do.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:30.64,1:28:33.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我的预言不能让他们听见\N{\rEN\blur0.8}My prophecy is not for their ears.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:34.43,1:28:35.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}回船上去\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Back to the ship.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:37.69,1:28:38.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}向西南航行\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Sail southwest.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:38.86,1:28:40.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}经过塞壬的领地\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Past the sirens.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:41.69,1:28:43.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}她们的歌声会引你的船员撞上礁石\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Their song lures your men onto the rocks.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:44.03,1:28:45.03,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们全都会死\N{\rEN\blur0.8}They all die.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:45.11,1:28:46.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我不会让那发生\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I won't let that happen.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:47.11,1:28:49.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我会用蜡堵住他们的耳朵\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'll block their ears. With wax.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:49.66,1:28:50.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}过了塞壬\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Past the sirens
Dialogue: 0,1:28:50.78,1:28:53.33,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你要在卡律布狄斯的漩涡\N{\rEN\blur0.8}you choose between the whirlpool Charybdis
Dialogue: 0,1:28:53.41,1:28:54.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}和怪物斯库拉之间做出选择\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and the monster Scylla.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:54.79,1:28:57.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}海中的漩涡会吞噬你们所有人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The whirlpool in the sea takes all of your lives.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:57.58,1:28:59.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}峭壁上的怪物 只会夺走六条命\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The monster in the cliffs, only six.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:59.96,1:29:01.63,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可你决意\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But your determination
Dialogue: 0,1:29:01.71,1:29:04.17,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不再牺牲任何人 反倒害死所有人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}to not sacrifice any more lives kills all of them.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:05.38,1:29:06.42,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我会做该做的事\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'll do what I have to.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:06.51,1:29:09.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}最后 饥饿与哗变迫在眉睫\N{\rEN\blur0.8}At the end, when starvation and mutiny threaten,
Dialogue: 0,1:29:09.43,1:29:13.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们要求登上太阳神放牧牛群的岛屿\N{\rEN\blur0.8}they demand to land where the Sun God grazes his cattle.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:13.72,1:29:15.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}宰杀阿波罗的牛群\N{\rEN\blur0.8}They slaughter Apollo's herd.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:16.68,1:29:18.31,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}宙斯因此取了他们的性命\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Zeus kills them for it.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:18.40,1:29:19.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}明白了吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Do you see?
Dialogue: 0,1:29:20.77,1:29:22.11,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我会阻止他们\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'll stop them.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:22.19,1:29:25.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}为何幸存者的性命 比比死去的人更重要？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Why do you value these men's lives more than those you've already lost?
Dialogue: 0,1:29:25.57,1:29:27.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我还能救他们 不让神明夺走他们\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I can still save them from the gods.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:27.70,1:29:30.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}却阻止不了他们自取灭亡\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But not from themselves.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:33.12,1:29:34.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那是什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What is that?
Dialogue: 0,1:29:34.24,1:29:35.83,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你那些未获安葬的船员\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Your unburied crew.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:39.37,1:29:41.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}要你与他们同受耻辱\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Demanding you share their dishonor.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:43.59,1:29:44.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}快走！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Let's go!
Dialogue: 0,1:30:00.44,1:30:01.73,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}解缆！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Cast off!
Dialogue: 0,1:30:02.52,1:30:04.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}解缆！ 快！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Cast off! Move it!
Dialogue: 0,1:30:29.72,1:30:30.76,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那就是我们的命运？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Is that our fate?
Dialogue: 0,1:30:33.64,1:30:35.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那就是我们的命运？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Is that our fate?
Dialogue: 0,1:30:55.95,1:30:58.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们划船离开冥府\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We rowed out of Hell,
Dialogue: 0,1:30:59.16,1:31:01.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}留下那么多战死的同伴\N{\rEN\blur0.8}leaving so many fallen comrades.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:02.42,1:31:04.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我必须救下剩下的人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I have to save the rest.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:04.96,1:31:06.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们后来怎么了？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What's happened to them?
Dialogue: 0,1:31:07.00,1:31:08.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们把我留在这里了？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Did they leave me here?
Dialogue: 0,1:31:08.38,1:31:10.01,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还会回来吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Are they coming back?
Dialogue: 0,1:31:11.92,1:31:13.55,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你对他们做了什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Did you do something to them?
Dialogue: 0,1:31:15.14,1:31:16.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你对他们做了什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Did you do something to them?
Dialogue: 0,1:31:16.93,1:31:18.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}吃一点\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Have some.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:18.72,1:31:20.93,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你说过不让我吃忘忧莲\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You told me not to eat the lotus flower.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:21.02,1:31:22.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就今晚\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Just tonight.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:22.89,1:31:24.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}让你好好睡一觉\N{\rEN\blur0.8}So you can get some sleep.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:27.86,1:31:31.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}明天天 等你准备好 就会想起来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And tomorrow, when you're ready, you'll remember.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:34.16,1:31:36.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}想起你的船员\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You'll remember your crew.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:36.37,1:31:37.83,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还有你的家人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And your family.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:37.91,1:31:39.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}家人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Family.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:40.87,1:31:42.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}妻子？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}A wife?
Dialogue: 0,1:31:43.83,1:31:45.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我有妻子吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Do I have a wife?
Dialogue: 0,1:31:49.84,1:31:52.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一你干什么？ 一没事 墨兰托\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What are you doing? It's all right, Melantho.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:52.80,1:31:54.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}外人不能进这里\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Strangers don't come in here.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:54.51,1:31:55.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不管有没有这道屏风\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Screen or no screen,
Dialogue: 0,1:31:55.80,1:31:59.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}共宴三年 我们早不是外人了 佩涅洛佩\N{\rEN\blur0.8}after three years of feasting together, we're far from strangers, Penelope.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:59.26,1:32:02.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你是想娶我 还是毁我名声？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Are you trying to marry me or ruin my reputation?
Dialogue: 0,1:32:02.60,1:32:03.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}墨兰托会守口如瓶\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Melantho can be discreet.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:04.35,1:32:07.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我正是担心你的名声 才来的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm actually here out of concern for your reputation.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:07.86,1:32:08.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh?
Dialogue: 0,1:32:08.94,1:32:10.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}大家都看得到你的辛劳\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Everyone sees how hard you work.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:10.65,1:32:13.19,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不疾不徐 一点点织着\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Slow, steady progress.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:13.28,1:32:14.49,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}嗯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Hmm...
Dialogue: 0,1:32:14.57,1:32:16.95,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可每晚 你又把织好的拆掉\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But, every night, you've been unraveling that work.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:22.75,1:32:23.79,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你先退下\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Leave us.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:23.87,1:32:26.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你总不能指望她\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You can't expect her
Dialogue: 0,1:32:26.79,1:32:29.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}忠于一个素未谋面的主人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}to be loyal to a master she never even knew.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:29.34,1:32:31.21,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我指望她忠于我\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I expect her to be loyal to me.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:31.30,1:32:32.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}她会的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And she will be.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:32.34,1:32:33.96,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}等你嫁给我之后\N{\rEN\blur0.8}When you're married to me.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:35.01,1:32:38.55,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}奴仆别无选择 只能忠于未来的主人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Slaves have no choice but to be loyal to the future
Dialogue: 0,1:32:38.64,1:32:40.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这座宅邸正在等待主人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and this is a household waiting for a master,
Dialogue: 0,1:32:40.93,1:32:43.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}正如伊萨卡正在等待国王\N{\rEN\blur0.8}just as Ithaca's a kingdom waiting for a king.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:45.94,1:32:47.73,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}伊萨卡的国王会回来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Ithaca's king is coming back.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:47.81,1:32:49.15,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他不会了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No, he's not.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:51.02,1:32:53.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你可知道 年少时我曾想随他去特洛伊？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Do you know that, as a boy, I tried to go with him to Troy?
Dialogue: 0,1:32:55.03,1:32:56.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他从没告诉过我\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He never told me that.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:57.82,1:32:59.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}奥德修斯不肯让我去\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Odysseus refused to let me.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:59.16,1:33:02.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他知道 伊萨卡必须有不依靠他的未来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He knew that Ithaca needed a future without him.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:09.38,1:33:11.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他认为 我也是那未来的一部分\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And he saw me as part of that future.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:16.22,1:33:21.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我不会向其他求婚者揭穿你的骗局\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'll never tell other suitors about your... Deception.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:23.68,1:33:25.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}把布织完吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Finish your weaving.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:27.23,1:33:28.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}该放下他了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's time to let him go.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:37.95,1:33:40.53,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}为什么想娶一个心里爱着别人的女人？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Why would you want to marry someone who loves someone else?
Dialogue: 0,1:33:43.54,1:33:48.21,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你对奥德修斯的忠贞 正是你的可贵之处\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Your loyalty to Odysseus is one of your finest qualities.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:51.54,1:33:52.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我爱你\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I love you.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:53.50,1:33:55.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我希望你选择我\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I want you to choose me.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:55.38,1:33:57.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}结束这一切\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-And end all this.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:58.26,1:34:00.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}别说你不累\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You can't tell me you're not tired.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:01.55,1:34:04.14,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}等待 悬而未决\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The waiting. The uncertainty.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:06.27,1:34:08.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你已尽到了责任\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You've done your duty.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:10.02,1:34:13.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一年 又一年\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Year after year after year.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:16.53,1:34:18.11,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}该替自己想想了心以儿\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's time to think of yourself.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:19.95,1:34:21.36,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}该重新生活了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's time to live again.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:26.87,1:34:28.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}奥德修斯也会这样希望\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's what Odysseus would've wanted.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:35.46,1:34:36.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我会满足你所有的需要\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'll take care of all your needs.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:41.63,1:34:42.76,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我的王后\N{\rEN\blur0.8}My Queen.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:45.89,1:34:47.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那我的儿子呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And my son?
Dialogue: 0,1:34:48.56,1:34:50.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}王位属于他\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The throne is his.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:50.10,1:34:51.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他是继承人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He's the heir.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:53.60,1:34:56.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}除非我们有了自己的孩子\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Unless we have a child of our own.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:06.20,1:35:07.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}忒勒马科斯在哪儿？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Where is Telemachus?
Dialogue: 0,1:35:09.29,1:35:10.75,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他去内陆了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He's gone inland.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:10.83,1:35:13.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一去看望祖父 一嗯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-To visit his grandfather.   -Hmm...
Dialogue: 0,1:35:20.46,1:35:21.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}她在说谎\N{\rEN\blur0.8}She's lying.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:22.01,1:35:23.47,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他出海了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He's gone to sea.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:37.94,1:35:39.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}去打听他父亲的下落\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He's gone for news of his father.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:40.28,1:35:41.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}去哪儿？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Where?
Dialogue: 0,1:35:41.36,1:35:43.95,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}去斯巴达 找墨涅拉俄斯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He's gone to Sparta. To Menelaus.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:45.28,1:35:46.74,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那我们也去？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, should we go there?
Dialogue: 0,1:35:47.53,1:35:48.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:49.87,1:35:53.21,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}太吵了 墨兰提俄斯 说了你只是牧牛人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Too loud, Melanthius. I told you you're a cowherd.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:54.33,1:35:55.67,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一他在偷听 一不 不\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He was listening. No, no.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:55.75,1:35:57.04,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不是\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No. No.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:59.42,1:36:00.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是来找阿尔戈斯的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I was coming for Argus.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:02.09,1:36:03.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我说过 那条狗就待在那里\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I told you that dog stays there.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:03.59,1:36:04.97,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}回农庄去\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Go back to the farm.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:05.05,1:36:06.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}需要猪时 我们会派墨兰提俄斯去取\N{\rEN\blur0.8}When we need your pigs, we'll send Melanthius.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:07.72,1:36:09.93,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}老头 这座王宫不再欢迎你\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You're no longer welcome in this palace, old man.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:10.01,1:36:11.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我只听女主人的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I answer to my mistress.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:14.31,1:36:15.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}她连你的名字都记得吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}She even know your name?
Dialogue: 0,1:36:17.15,1:36:18.19,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}滚吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now go.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:18.77,1:36:22.03,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}忒勒马科斯回程 必经皮洛斯的神庙\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Telemachus will have to come back by the temple at Pylos.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:22.90,1:36:24.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}带上你的人 去去那里等他\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Take your men and wait for him there.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:24.49,1:36:26.74,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好让你留下讨好王后？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Why, so you can stay and try and charm the Queen?
Dialogue: 0,1:36:26.82,1:36:28.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}想都别想\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't think so.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:29.08,1:36:30.74,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他必须死在那条路上\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He needs to die on that road.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:30.83,1:36:32.45,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}伊罗斯已经有了计划\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And Irus has a plan.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:33.25,1:36:34.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}伊罗斯！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}lrus!
Dialogue: 0,1:36:36.75,1:36:38.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他一行人 我要一个不留\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I need everyone in his party dead.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:38.54,1:36:40.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}割开喉咙 扔进沟里\N{\rEN\blur0.8}In a ditch. Throats open.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:40.63,1:36:43.05,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}忒勒马科斯和他的人会提防强盗\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Telemachus and his men will be ready for the bandits
Dialogue: 0,1:36:43.13,1:36:45.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那些在这里到皮洛斯的路上打劫的强盗\N{\rEN\blur0.8}who work the road between here and Pylos.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:46.43,1:36:48.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可要是有人先从祭司手里夺下神庙\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But if some of them took the temple from the priests
Dialogue: 0,1:36:48.80,1:36:49.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}在他们赶到之前-\N{\rEN\blur0.8}before they arrived...
Dialogue: 0,1:36:51.26,1:36:53.31,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}再带回忒勒马科斯身上的东西作证\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And bring me part of Telemachus as proof.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:54.81,1:36:55.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他的鼻子\N{\rEN\blur0.8}His nose.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:56.52,1:36:58.31,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}光凭鼻子 你认得出是他？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Would you know him only by his nose?
Dialogue: 0,1:37:01.90,1:37:03.15,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那就再加上耳朵\N{\rEN\blur0.8}His ears too.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:08.36,1:37:09.99,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}谁教你的？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Who taught you?
Dialogue: 0,1:37:10.07,1:37:11.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我父亲的牧猪人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}My father's swineherd.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:11.70,1:37:12.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那个牧猪人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The swineherder.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:12.87,1:37:14.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}对 他最忠心的仆人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yeah, his most loyal servant.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:15.08,1:37:18.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}奥德修斯把最忠心的仆人留在了家里\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Odysseus left his most loyal servant behind.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:18.17,1:37:19.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他向来最聪明\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He always was the smartest.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:20.63,1:37:23.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}阿伽门农只听得进他的话\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Only one Agamemnon ever listened to.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:23.84,1:37:25.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可惜听得还不够\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Should have listened harder.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:25.42,1:37:27.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我能问问你哥哥遭遇了什么吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Can I ask what happened to your brother?
Dialogue: 0,1:37:27.34,1:37:28.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他妻子背叛了他\N{\rEN\blur0.8}His wife betrayed him.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:28.68,1:37:29.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}谋杀了他\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Murdered him.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:30.51,1:37:31.55,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你怎么处置他们的？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What did you do to them?
Dialogue: 0,1:37:31.64,1:37:33.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他儿子俄瑞斯忒斯杀了那两个人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}His son Orestes, he killed them both.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:34.68,1:37:36.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}什么？ 他杀了自己的母亲？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What, he killed his own mother?
Dialogue: 0,1:37:37.31,1:37:38.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他替父亲报了仇\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He avenged his father.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:39.44,1:37:40.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不过你不用担心\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But you don't have to worry.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:40.90,1:37:43.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你母亲和克吕泰涅斯特拉截然不同\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Your mother has nothing in common with Clytemnestra.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:43.69,1:37:44.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也许吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Maybe not.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:44.78,1:37:46.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可求婚者已经说服了长老们\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But the suitors have convinced the elders
Dialogue: 0,1:37:46.69,1:37:48.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}说她该改嫁了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-it's time she remarried.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:48.90,1:37:50.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}眼下可不是让王位空悬的时候\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's not a good time for an empty throne.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:51.41,1:37:53.53,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}传闻你听说过吧 那些来自海上的人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You've heard the stories. People from the sea.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:53.62,1:37:54.79,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们遭到袭击了吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Have you been raided?
Dialogue: 0,1:37:54.87,1:37:57.29,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还没有 但他们似乎越来越近了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Not yet, but the attacks, they do seem closer.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:57.37,1:37:58.75,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}斯巴达已经做好准备\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Sparta's ready.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:58.83,1:38:00.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}伊萨卡呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What about Ithaca?
Dialogue: 0,1:38:00.67,1:38:02.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}她能召集军队保护自己吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Would she be able to raise an army, defend herself?
Dialogue: 0,1:38:03.00,1:38:04.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}总得有人继承王位\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Someone's gotta take the throne.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:04.46,1:38:06.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那么孩子 你的战场在那里 不在这里\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, then the battle is there, not here, son.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:07.72,1:38:09.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你逃避了问题\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You've run from the problem.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:10.22,1:38:12.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}把母亲留下 任那些求婚者摆布\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And left your mother at the mercy of the suitors.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:14.06,1:38:15.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我该雇些佣兵吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Should I hire mercenaries?
Dialogue: 0,1:38:15.97,1:38:18.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}回去把他们全杀了？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Go back and kill them all?
Dialogue: 0,1:38:18.31,1:38:20.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}在自己家里谋杀有权有势的客人？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Murder rich and powerful guests in your own home?
Dialogue: 0,1:38:21.10,1:38:22.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你会被流放\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You'd be exiled.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:22.65,1:38:24.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那该怎么办？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What then?
Dialogue: 0,1:38:24.32,1:38:27.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你必须赶走他们 又不违背宙斯的律法\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You must evict them without violating Zeus' Law.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:29.32,1:38:30.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我得继承王位\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I have to take the throne.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:32.20,1:38:34.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我得知道奥德修斯是否还活着\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I have to know if Odysseus is alive.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:34.66,1:38:37.33,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这与你素未谋面的父亲无关\N{\rEN\blur0.8}This is nothing to do with a father you've never known.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:37.95,1:38:39.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}孩子 你必须承担领导之责\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You have to lead, son.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:39.79,1:38:41.33,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}无论奥德修斯遭遇了什么\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No matter what's happened to Odysseus.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:55.60,1:38:56.97,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你得想起来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You need to remember.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:57.06,1:38:58.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不 我不需要\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No, I don't.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:59.27,1:39:01.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我不需要知道真相 在这里和你一起 我很快乐\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't need to know the truth. I'm happy here. With you.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:04.27,1:39:08.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那你为何要捡回旧船的残骸造木筏？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Then why are you gathering the bones of your old ship to make a raft?
Dialogue: 0,1:39:10.78,1:39:12.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}想想你的船员\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Remember your crew.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:13.70,1:39:14.74,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你的旅程\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Your journey.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:18.79,1:39:21.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我听过塞壬的歌声\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I heard the song of the sirens.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:30.84,1:39:32.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}用蜡堵住他们的耳朵\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Put the wax in the men's ears.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:33.68,1:39:36.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一我不用 把我绑在桅杆上 一为什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-None for me. Tie me to the mast.   -Why?
Dialogue: 0,1:39:36.51,1:39:37.97,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我想听塞壬唱歌\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I wanna hear the sirens' song.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:38.06,1:39:38.97,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不行\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:39.93,1:39:41.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这可不是好主意\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's a bad idea.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:41.31,1:39:42.73,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没人听过那歌声还能活命\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No one's ever heard the song and lived.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:42.81,1:39:45.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}所以才是好主意 我会是第一个\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's why it's a good idea. I'll be the first.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:46.19,1:39:47.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}无论我怎么哀求\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No matter how hard I plead,
Dialogue: 0,1:39:47.65,1:39:50.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没远远离开之前 都不准松绑\N{\rEN\blur0.8}do not untie me until we're well clear.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:51.32,1:39:52.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}检查他们的耳朵\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Check the men's ears.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:53.61,1:39:56.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}谁先回答一声遵命 赏赏一星期口粮！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}A week's rations for the first, "Yes, sir"!
Dialogue: 0,1:40:31.36,1:40:32.36,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}啊\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh...
Dialogue: 0,1:40:54.88,1:40:56.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}塞壬唱的是什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What was the sirens' song?
Dialogue: 0,1:40:57.68,1:40:59.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你渴望听到的一切\N{\rEN\blur0.8}All the things you want it to be.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:00.56,1:41:04.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}然后是你宁愿从未渴望过的一切\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Then all the things you wish you never wished for.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:22.16,1:41:25.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就像一阵舒爽的痒 你伸手去挠\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It was the delicious itch you go to scratch,
Dialogue: 0,1:41:26.50,1:41:29.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}却发现它在皮肤下面 怎么也挠不到\N{\rEN\blur0.8}but find it's under the skin. You can' reach it.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:31.29,1:41:34.05,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那舒爽的痒 于是变得难以忍受\N{\rEN\blur0.8}So the delicious itch becomes unbearable.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:38.34,1:41:40.47,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}它告诉你 最渴望的东西\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Told you what you most want
Dialogue: 0,1:41:42.47,1:41:44.47,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}恰恰是最无法得到的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}is what you most can't have.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:48.06,1:41:49.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}而最无法得到的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And what you most can't have
Dialogue: 0,1:41:51.19,1:41:53.36,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}恰恰是你曾经拥有过\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Is what you already had.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:53.44,1:41:55.03,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}却又失去的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And lost.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:03.28,1:42:05.83,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}它唱出了我所有未能兑现的承诺\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It was the song of all the promises I failed to keep.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:11.17,1:42:13.63,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还告诉我 其实我并不想回家\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And it told me I don't really wanna go home.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:16.67,1:42:18.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}激流！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}White water!
Dialogue: 0,1:42:18.67,1:42:19.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}前面有激流！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}White water ahead!
Dialogue: 0,1:42:22.64,1:42:23.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}卡律布狄斯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Charybdis.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:24.72,1:42:26.39,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一个骇人的巨漩涡\N{\rEN\blur0.8}A monstrous whirlpool.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:29.10,1:42:30.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}升帆！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Hoist the sails!
Dialogue: 0,1:42:30.77,1:42:32.19,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}快 动起来！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Come on, let's go!
Dialogue: 0,1:42:32.27,1:42:34.15,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}转动绞盘！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Get the windlass up!
Dialogue: 0,1:42:34.23,1:42:35.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}能驶向外海吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Can we head out to sea?
Dialogue: 0,1:42:35.65,1:42:36.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们已经被卷进去了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's already got us.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:38.94,1:42:40.36,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}拉住那些绳索！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Man those ropes!
Dialogue: 0,1:42:40.45,1:42:42.24,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们要往北 快！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We wanna head north! Move it!
Dialogue: 0,1:42:43.53,1:42:45.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一也许能穿过那条峡谷 一太窄了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-We might make that canyon.   -It's too narrow.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:45.66,1:42:47.45,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}朝漩涡开\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Make for the whirlpool.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:47.54,1:42:49.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}顺着水势往下驶\N{\rEN\blur0.8}If you steer down the slope,
Dialogue: 0,1:42:49.16,1:42:51.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就能借着冲力 从另一侧冲出去\N{\rEN\blur0.8}we can make enough way to shoot out the other side.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:51.67,1:42:53.33,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}别怕 我们能做到\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Don't be afraid. We can do it.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:58.34,1:43:00.17,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不 不行！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No. No!
Dialogue: 0,1:43:00.88,1:43:02.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们走水道\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We're making for the channel.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:02.38,1:43:04.14,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一冷静点 一我们走水道！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Get a grip.   -We're making for the channel!
Dialogue: 0,1:43:04.22,1:43:05.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}收桨！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oars in!
Dialogue: 0,1:43:07.31,1:43:08.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}把桨收进来！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Get the oars in!
Dialogue: 0,1:43:09.10,1:43:11.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}右舷船桨 准备抵水！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Starboard oars, prepare to hold water!
Dialogue: 0,1:43:18.48,1:43:19.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}听我号令！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}On my signal!
Dialogue: 0,1:43:21.11,1:43:22.11,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}三\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Three...
Dialogue: 0,1:43:24.32,1:43:25.45,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}二\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Two...
Dialogue: 0,1:43:26.83,1:43:28.33,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}用力！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}One! Hard!
Dialogue: 0,1:43:29.66,1:43:32.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}出桨！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oars out!
Dialogue: 0,1:43:42.09,1:43:43.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}稳住！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Hold it!
Dialogue: 0,1:44:16.71,1:44:18.21,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们过来了！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We made it!
Dialogue: 0,1:44:18.29,1:44:19.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}过来了！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We did!
Dialogue: 0,1:44:20.21,1:44:22.09,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们成功了 诸神保佑我们……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We did it. The gods were with us...
Dialogue: 0,1:44:25.80,1:44:26.76,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}划！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Pull!
Dialogue: 0,1:44:28.18,1:44:29.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}划！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Pull!
Dialogue: 0,1:44:29.93,1:44:32.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}划！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Pull!
Dialogue: 0,1:44:32.85,1:44:34.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}保持航向！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Keep us straight!
Dialogue: 0,1:44:36.94,1:44:38.36,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}划！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Pull!
Dialogue: 0,1:44:40.48,1:44:41.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}划！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Pull!
Dialogue: 0,1:44:41.86,1:44:43.15,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}保持航向！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Keep us straight!
Dialogue: 0,1:44:43.24,1:44:46.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}划！ 划！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Pull! Pull!
Dialogue: 0,1:44:49.07,1:44:50.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}划！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Pull!
Dialogue: 0,1:45:10.22,1:45:11.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你早就知道\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You knew.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:11.76,1:45:12.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}却没告诉我们\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And you didn't tell us.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:13.68,1:45:15.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}告诉你 你们就不会走这条路\N{\rEN\blur0.8}If I told you, you wouldn't have chosen this way.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:15.89,1:45:17.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那他们就还活着！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And those men would still be alive!
Dialogue: 0,1:45:17.98,1:45:18.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No!
Dialogue: 0,1:45:19.06,1:45:20.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们都会死\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We'd all be dead.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:20.61,1:45:22.15,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你没这个权力！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You had no right!
Dialogue: 0,1:45:22.23,1:45:23.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我当然有\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I had every right.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:23.65,1:45:25.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也有这个责任！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And every responsibility!
Dialogue: 0,1:45:25.36,1:45:28.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那漩涡会毁掉船 把我们全吞下去\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The whirlpool would have destroyed the ship and all of us.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:28.49,1:45:29.53,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}走这里 我们才能活\N{\rEN\blur0.8}This way, we live.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:29.62,1:45:30.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}只是有些人能活！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Some of us live!
Dialogue: 0,1:45:30.78,1:45:32.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没错！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yes!
Dialogue: 0,1:45:35.50,1:45:36.96,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}忒瑞西阿斯还告诉了你什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What else did Tiresias tell you?
Dialogue: 0,1:45:49.05,1:45:50.47,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我要在那里靠岸\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm gonna put in there.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:52.89,1:45:56.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不能上那座岛 那是太阳神的岛\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We can't land there. That's the Sun God's isle.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:56.27,1:45:57.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们得修船\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We need repairs.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:58.85,1:46:00.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}大家都筋疲力尽了！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}These men are exhausted!
Dialogue: 0,1:46:00.69,1:46:01.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们刚死了六个同伴！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We lost six shipmates!
Dialogue: 0,1:46:02.56,1:46:05.15,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们要靠岸 踏踏实实地歇一歇\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We're gonna put in. We're gonna rest up on dry land.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:05.23,1:46:07.24,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们全都会死！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-You're all gonna die!
Dialogue: 0,1:46:09.82,1:46:11.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你不是问忒瑞西阿斯说了什么吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You asked me what Tiresias told me?
Dialogue: 0,1:46:12.74,1:46:14.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他说 你们全都会死\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He said you're all gonna die.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:14.95,1:46:20.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}如果你们宰杀那岛上太阳神的牛\N{\rEN\blur0.8}If you slaughter the Sun God's cattle which graze on that island.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:20.16,1:46:21.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就全都会死\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You'll all die.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:25.59,1:46:26.63,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那好办\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's fine.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:27.59,1:46:28.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们靠岸\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We'll put in.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:29.42,1:46:30.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}只煮自己带的食物\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We'll cook our own provisions.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:30.76,1:46:33.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}摘果子 取水 仅此而已\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We'll pick fruit. We'll get water. Nothing more.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:35.14,1:46:36.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}发誓\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Swear to it.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:37.06,1:46:38.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们所有人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}All of you.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:52.03,1:46:53.03,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}看吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}See?
Dialogue: 0,1:46:54.03,1:46:55.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}风直接把我们送来了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The wind took us right in.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:56.70,1:46:59.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}歇一歇 把船修好\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We'll rest up. Do the repairs.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:59.75,1:47:02.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}风向一变 我们就走\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We'll set out as soon as the wind changes.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:02.75,1:47:03.75,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}抓住那根绳子\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Grab that line.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:14.93,1:47:16.93,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}船员们守诺了吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Did the crew keep their promise?
Dialogue: 0,1:47:17.97,1:47:19.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}守了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yes.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:19.72,1:47:21.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}守了很久\N{\rEN\blur0.8}For a long time.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:22.69,1:47:24.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可风向一直没变\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But the wind never changed.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:24.31,1:47:28.36,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那股让我们轻松靠岸的向岸风\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The steady, on-shore breeze that made it so easy for us to land
Dialogue: 0,1:47:30.86,1:47:32.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一直不停 让我们无法离开\N{\rEN\blur0.8}made it impossible to leave.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:36.41,1:47:38.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们的食物也吃光了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And our provisions ran out.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:41.58,1:47:42.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}去吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Go.
Dialogue: 0,1:48:45.27,1:48:48.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}以为吃的时候不出声 太阳神就不知道？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Did you think if you ate quietly the Sun God wouldn't notice?
Dialogue: 0,1:48:48.56,1:48:50.27,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们以为你不会知道\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We thought you wouldn't notice.
Dialogue: 0,1:48:50.90,1:48:52.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}问题不在我\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm not the problem.
Dialogue: 0,1:48:52.48,1:48:54.11,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是想让你们活下来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I wanted you to live.
Dialogue: 0,1:48:59.78,1:49:01.24,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}忒瑞西阿斯提醒过你\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Tiresias told you.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:01.33,1:49:03.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}喀耳刻提醒过你 诸神也提醒过你\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Circe told you. The gods told you.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:04.25,1:49:06.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们诸神说的话 我们听不懂\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You gods don't speak in ways we understand.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:06.79,1:49:08.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}谁会不懂痛苦？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Who doesn't understand pain?
Dialogue: 0,1:49:09.29,1:49:10.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不懂流血 不懂死亡？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Or blood or death?
Dialogue: 0,1:49:11.54,1:49:14.63,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}看着部下死去 你看到的是意外还是后果？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}When you watch your men die, do you see chance or do you see consequence?
Dialogue: 0,1:49:15.17,1:49:17.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是后果 是我的失职\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I see consequence. I see my failure.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:18.34,1:49:21.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}如果他们的死 是他们自己的过错呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What if their deaths aren't your failure but theirs?
Dialogue: 0,1:49:21.14,1:49:22.39,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是他们的首领\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I lead them.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:23.81,1:49:25.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是我带他们来的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I led them here.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:25.43,1:49:26.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那又是谁引领你？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And who led you?
Dialogue: 0,1:49:27.94,1:49:29.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你为何自居于诸神之上？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Why do you put yourself above the gods?
Dialogue: 0,1:49:29.60,1:49:31.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}为何认定一切都是你的责任？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Why do you claim responsibility?
Dialogue: 0,1:49:32.40,1:49:34.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你为什么不想回家？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Why don't you wanna go home?
Dialogue: 0,1:49:34.15,1:49:35.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你还想怎样？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What do you expect?
Dialogue: 0,1:49:37.28,1:49:38.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们已经没吃的了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}They ran out of food.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:39.82,1:49:40.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}发发慈悲吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Have some pity.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:40.91,1:49:43.83,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就是我的慈悲 让我们来了这该死的岛\N{\rEN\blur0.8}My pity is what put us on this damned island.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:43.91,1:49:45.24,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我说过会有什么后果\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I told you what would happen.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:45.33,1:49:46.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}对 你说过\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yes, you did.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:47.16,1:49:50.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们决定 宁可淹死 也不饿死\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And we decided we would rather drown than starve.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:55.76,1:49:57.97,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}机会来了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, now's our chance.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:58.05,1:50:00.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}风停了！ 风停了！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The wind has dropped! The wind has dropped!
Dialogue: 0,1:50:04.26,1:50:08.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那片刻的平静 恰好将我们诱入波塞冬之海\N{\rEN\blur0.8}7he calm was just long enough fo lure us out onto Poseidon's ocean.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:09.35,1:50:11.19,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}宙斯的苍穹之下\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Under Zeus' sky.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:11.27,1:50:14.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}把船转向迎风！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Get us into the wind!
Dialogue: 0,1:50:14.48,1:50:16.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}左舷！ 左舷！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Port! Port!
Dialogue: 0,1:50:30.29,1:50:31.79,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}向诸神祈祷！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Pray to the gods!
Dialogue: 0,1:50:32.92,1:50:35.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一把船转向迎风！ 一祈求宽恕！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Get us into the wind! Pray for forgiveness!
Dialogue: 0,1:50:35.92,1:50:37.17,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}迎风！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Wind!
Dialogue: 0,1:50:52.81,1:50:54.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}把船转向迎风！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Get us into the wind!
Dialogue: 0,1:50:55.44,1:50:56.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}迎风！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Into the wind!
Dialogue: 0,1:50:59.57,1:51:01.11,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}奥德修斯！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Odysseus!
Dialogue: 0,1:51:02.74,1:51:04.24,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}把船转向迎风！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Get us into the wind!
Dialogue: 0,1:51:17.75,1:51:19.63,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}把自己交给诸神！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Give yourself to the gods!
Dialogue: 0,1:51:23.64,1:51:25.93,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}向波塞冬祈祷！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Pray to Poseidon!
Dialogue: 0,1:51:32.39,1:51:34.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}祈求宽恕！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Pray for forgiveness!
Dialogue: 0,1:51:46.78,1:51:47.95,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}小心！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Look out!
Dialogue: 0,1:52:02.97,1:52:05.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我最后记得的 是宙斯那无情的一击\N{\rEN\blur0.8}7Jhe last thing I remember was the harsh hand of Zeus.
Dialogue: 0,1:52:18.32,1:52:20.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}欧律洛科斯！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Eurylochus!
Dialogue: 0,1:52:50.85,1:52:52.27,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我不知道我的人怎么样了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't know what happened to my men.
Dialogue: 0,1:52:52.35,1:52:53.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你知道\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yes, you do.
Dialogue: 0,1:52:55.64,1:52:57.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就和你警告过他们的一样\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Exactly what you told them would happen.
Dialogue: 0,1:52:57.94,1:52:59.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我独自漂到了你的岸边\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I washed up on your shore alone.
Dialogue: 0,1:52:59.98,1:53:02.36,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你漂到了我的岸边\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You washed up on my shore
Dialogue: 0,1:53:02.44,1:53:04.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}带着些船的残骸 却没有一个船员\N{\rEN\blur0.8}with some of your boat and none of your crew.
Dialogue: 0,1:53:06.95,1:53:09.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}奄奄一息 昏迷不醒\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Half dead, unconscious.
Dialogue: 0,1:53:31.47,1:53:33.97,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我看着你 昏迷了好几天……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}/ watched you lost for days...
Dialogue: 0,1:53:34.06,1:53:35.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不 不 不\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No, no, no.
Dialogue: 0,1:53:35.93,1:53:37.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}又过了好几周\N{\rEN\blur0.8}...lnfo weeks.
Dialogue: 0,1:53:38.27,1:53:40.15,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我知道忘忧莲能让你醒来时好受些\N{\rEN\blur0.8}/ knew the lotus would ease your awakening.
Dialogue: 0,1:53:40.23,1:53:42.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不 不 不\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No, no, no.
Dialogue: 0,1:53:42.61,1:53:45.32,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}让你更多感到身体的疼 而非心里的痛\N{\rEN\blur0.8}So that your pain was more of the body than the mind.
Dialogue: 0,1:53:48.07,1:53:49.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}它确实做到了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And it did.
Dialogue: 0,1:53:51.74,1:53:53.49,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你那么喜欢它\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You liked it so much.
Dialogue: 0,1:53:54.66,1:53:56.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那么乐意吃下去\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You ate it so willingly.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:00.33,1:54:01.75,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}而我照顾你的时候……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And as I cared for you...
Dialogue: 0,1:54:02.38,1:54:03.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}谢谢你\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:03.59,1:54:05.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也爱上了你\N{\rEN\blur0.8}.../ came to love you.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:10.55,1:54:12.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我在这里多久了？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}How long have I been here?
Dialogue: 0,1:54:14.35,1:54:17.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我一直告诉自己 别再给你吃了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I kept telling myself to stop giving it to you,
Dialogue: 0,1:54:17.10,1:54:19.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你已经能承受那些回忆\N{\rEN\blur0.8}that you were strong enough to remember.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:19.14,1:54:21.27,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-多久了 卡吕普索？  -可是你那么快乐\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-How long, Calypso?   -I mean, you were so happy.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:21.36,1:54:24.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一你很快乐 一我们都很快乐 好多年了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-You were happy.   -We were so happy. For years.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:24.98,1:54:26.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好多年？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Years?
Dialogue: 0,1:54:32.99,1:54:33.99,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}七年\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Seven years.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:35.24,1:54:38.83,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你给我吃忘忧莲 把我囚禁在这里\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You fed me lotus flower and held me captive.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:38.91,1:54:40.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我救了你的命\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I saved your life.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:41.29,1:54:42.33,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我治好了你的身体\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I rebuilt your body.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:42.42,1:54:45.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}却始终不忍让你找回记忆\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I just couldn't bring myself to rebuild your mind.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:46.50,1:54:48.05,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你一直很快乐\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You have been happy.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:49.13,1:54:52.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}只是你的心 始终在别处\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Your heart was just always somewhere else.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:53.47,1:54:57.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你的思绪迟早也会追随它而去\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And your mind was bound to follow eventually.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:57.93,1:54:59.27,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你怎么能这样？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}How could you?
Dialogue: 0,1:54:59.35,1:55:02.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}忘忧莲会蒙蔽心智 消磨意志\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The lotus clouds the mind and saps the will,
Dialogue: 0,1:55:02.60,1:55:04.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}却改变不了你是谁\N{\rEN\blur0.8}but it doesn't change who you are.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:05.19,1:55:08.03,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不管为何 那时你还没准备好回家\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You weren't ready to go home, for whatever reason.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:08.11,1:55:09.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}现在我准备好了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I am now.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:11.28,1:55:13.03,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我早知道会有这一天\N{\rEN\blur0.8}As I always knew you would be.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:13.66,1:55:14.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你怎么知道？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}How?
Dialogue: 0,1:55:14.74,1:55:17.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}发现你时 你手里紧着一样东西\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You were clutching something when I found you.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:17.74,1:55:19.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}几个星期都不肯松手\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Your hand wouldn''t open for weeks.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:20.37,1:55:21.75,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你会喊出声\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You'd call out.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:21.83,1:55:23.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}大多在呼唤雅典娜\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Mostly to Athena,
Dialogue: 0,1:55:23.58,1:55:26.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}但有时 你会喊另一个名字\N{\rEN\blur0.8}but sometimes you would say another name.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:40.60,1:55:42.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}佩涅洛佩\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Penelope.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:45.98,1:55:47.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}帮我回家\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Help me go home.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:48.11,1:55:49.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我正在帮你\N{\rEN\blur0.8}lam.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:50.53,1:55:53.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你是个非要掌控命运的人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You're aman who needs to control his fate.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:54.57,1:55:56.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可这件事 由不得你掌控\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But you cannot control this.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:59.41,1:56:01.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你必须把自己交给风暴\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You must give yourself to the storm.
Dialogue: 0,1:56:02.29,1:56:03.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}交给波塞冬\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Give yourself to Poseidon.
Dialogue: 0,1:56:05.38,1:56:06.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}接受你的惩罚\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And take your punishment.
Dialogue: 0,1:56:09.67,1:56:11.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}宙斯不会让他杀死你\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Zeus wont let him kill you.
Dialogue: 0,1:56:14.88,1:56:18.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}放弃抵抗 放弃掌控 才能活下来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Give up the fight, give up control, and live.
Dialogue: 0,1:56:21.18,1:56:25.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}奥德修斯 你还从未这样放手去信任过\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's a leap of faith you've never yet made, Odysseus.
Dialogue: 0,1:57:17.07,1:57:18.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}奥德修斯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Odysseus.
Dialogue: 0,1:57:26.33,1:57:27.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这是哪里？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Where am I?
Dialogue: 0,1:57:29.50,1:57:31.29,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}连自己的家都认不出来了？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Don't you recognize your own home?
Dialogue: 0,1:58:10.71,1:58:12.75,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}陌生人 宙斯欢迎你们\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Zeus welcomes you, strangers.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:13.54,1:58:14.55,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们有几个人？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}How many are you?
Dialogue: 0,1:58:15.13,1:58:16.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}六个\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Half a dozen.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:16.84,1:58:17.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}需要吃顿饭吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}In need of a meal?
Dialogue: 0,1:58:18.01,1:58:19.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还要些物资\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And supplies.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:20.01,1:58:21.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}路上用\N{\rEN\blur0.8}For the road.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:21.26,1:58:22.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们去哪儿？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Where you headed?
Dialogue: 0,1:58:22.60,1:58:24.01,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们需要猪\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We need pigs.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:24.10,1:58:25.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们要一路去皮洛斯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We're going all the way to Pylos.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:25.89,1:58:27.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们是朝圣者？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Are you pilgrims?
Dialogue: 0,1:58:27.85,1:58:29.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们看着像吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Do we look like pilgrims?
Dialogue: 0,1:58:29.89,1:58:31.27,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我眼神不好\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't see well.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:32.48,1:58:35.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}遵照宙斯的律法 我请你们吃饭 但这些猪不归我卖\N{\rEN\blur0.8}As Zeus demands, I offer you a meal but these pigs aren't mine to sell.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:36.07,1:58:37.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}别担心\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, don't worry.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:37.94,1:58:38.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们没打算付钱\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We're not paying.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:42.45,1:58:44.83,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}替我问候你母亲\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Give my greetings to your mother.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:47.87,1:58:49.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}告诉她 我很抱歉\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Tell her I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:49.50,1:58:50.96,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}为特洛伊的一切\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm sorry for Troy
Dialogue: 0,1:58:51.04,1:58:53.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}为所有因我之名而发生的事\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and for everything that has happened in my name.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:59.84,1:59:02.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}很抱歉 我没能告诉你父亲的下落\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm sorry I had no news of your father.
Dialogue: 0,1:59:02.38,1:59:03.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不 你已经告诉我了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No, you had news.
Dialogue: 0,1:59:03.51,1:59:06.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不是他的下落 而是他的为人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Not of where he is, but who he is.
Dialogue: 0,1:59:07.10,1:59:09.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}现在 我比以往更盼着有朝一日见到他\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And now, more than ever, I hope to one day meet him.
Dialogue: 0,1:59:14.77,1:59:16.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}老头 你的看门狗呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Where are your watchdogs, old man?
Dialogue: 0,1:59:21.32,1:59:23.45,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我正在烧它们的尸体\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm burning their bodies.
Dialogue: 0,1:59:27.74,1:59:30.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}陌生人 可愿接受宙斯款待的酒食？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Can Zeus offer you food and drink, stranger?
Dialogue: 0,1:59:31.50,1:59:33.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你遭人袭击了？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Were you attacked?
Dialogue: 0,1:59:33.21,1:59:35.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那些狗救了你的伙计\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The dogs saved your farmhands.
Dialogue: 0,1:59:35.08,1:59:37.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没有 我们先烧了他的兄弟们\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No, we burned his brothers first.
Dialogue: 0,1:59:40.38,1:59:42.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}伊萨卡怎么会变成这样？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What has happened to Ithaca?
Dialogue: 0,1:59:42.38,1:59:43.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}黑暗降临了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Darkness.
Dialogue: 0,1:59:43.47,1:59:46.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}宙斯的律法被践踏得粉碎\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Zeus' Law smashed to pieces.
Dialogue: 0,1:59:47.14,1:59:50.31,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}主人死后 这王国就没了国王\N{\rEN\blur0.8}A kingdom without a king since my master died.
Dialogue: 0,1:59:50.39,1:59:51.39,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你的主人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Your master.
Dialogue: 0,1:59:52.44,1:59:53.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}奥德修斯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Odysseus.
Dialogue: 0,1:59:53.94,1:59:55.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}特洛伊战争的英雄\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Hero of the Trojan War.
Dialogue: 0,1:59:58.36,1:59:59.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可奥德修斯还活着\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But Odysseus is alive.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:00.07,2:00:01.99,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}又是乞弓 只会让人空欢喜！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Beggars giving false hope!
Dialogue: 0,2:00:02.07,2:00:04.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}别再说了！ 别再说了！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No more! No more!
Dialogue: 0,2:00:04.24,2:00:06.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}别再说了 别说了 别说了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No more! No more. No more.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:06.78,2:00:08.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}别说了 别说了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No more. No more.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:08.28,2:00:11.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}忒勒马科斯 忒勒马科斯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Telemachus. Telemachus.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:11.45,2:00:12.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}忒勒马科斯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Telemachus.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:12.54,2:00:15.79,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他有危险 我却帮不了他\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He's in danger, and I can't help him.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:15.88,2:00:19.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}伊萨卡总还有别人愿意帮奥德修斯的儿子\N{\rEN\blur0.8}There must be others in Ithaca that would help Odysseus' son.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:19.59,2:00:22.05,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}王宫被求婚者把持着\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The palace is controlled by suitors.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:22.63,2:00:25.14,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}再没人忠于奥德修斯了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No one's still loyal to Odysseus.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:26.34,2:00:27.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}王后呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What about the Queen?
Dialogue: 0,2:00:28.30,2:00:30.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}美丽而睿智的佩涅洛佩\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Beautiful, wise Penelope.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:31.43,2:00:33.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}被最卑劣的人扣为人质\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Held hostage by the worst men.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:33.85,2:00:36.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}很快就会被逼改嫁\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Soon to be forced into marriage.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:36.19,2:00:38.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}连儿子都不在身边 她又能怎样？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What could she do without even her son?
Dialogue: 0,2:00:38.65,2:00:39.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}来 喝点\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Here. Drink.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:44.11,2:00:46.32,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}忒勒马科斯有什么危险？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-What's the danger to Telemachus?
Dialogue: 0,2:00:47.36,2:00:49.53,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他正在从斯巴达回来的路上\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He's on his way back from Sparta.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:50.74,2:00:55.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}求婚者派强盗去了皮洛斯 要在神庙伏击他\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The suitors sent bandits to Pylos to ambush him at the temple.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:56.25,2:00:57.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}给我点路上吃的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Give me food for the road.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:58.21,2:01:01.04,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你你追不上那些强盗的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You'll... You'll never catch up with the bandits.
Dialogue: 0,2:01:01.13,2:01:04.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}只要赶在忒勒马科斯之前到皮洛斯 就能提醒他\N{\rEN\blur0.8}If I can get to Pylos before Telemachus arrives, I can warn him.
Dialogue: 0,2:01:05.01,2:01:06.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你为什么愿意帮忙？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Why are you helping?
Dialogue: 0,2:01:07.34,2:01:09.05,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}说了 你可别生气\N{\rEN\blur0.8}If I tell you, don't be angry.
Dialogue: 0,2:01:09.85,2:01:11.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我曾随奥德修斯 在特洛伊作战\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I served with Odysseus. At Troy.
Dialogue: 0,2:01:11.64,2:01:12.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}真的？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Really?
Dialogue: 0,2:01:14.10,2:01:15.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他治军严苛\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He was a harsh taskmaster.
Dialogue: 0,2:01:15.68,2:01:16.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可他公正\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Ah, but fair.
Dialogue: 0,2:01:18.23,2:01:20.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}公正 值得追随\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Fair and worthy of following.
Dialogue: 0,2:01:21.57,2:01:22.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你爱他吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You loved him?
Dialogue: 0,2:01:23.65,2:01:24.99,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就像自己的儿子\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Like a son.
Dialogue: 0,2:01:25.65,2:01:28.03,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他还没死\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, he's not dead.
Dialogue: 0,2:01:28.53,2:01:30.74,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他他要回家了吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Is... Is he coming home?
Dialogue: 0,2:01:30.82,2:01:32.04,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}快了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Soon.
Dialogue: 0,2:01:32.62,2:01:34.79,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}带着复仇而来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Bringing vengeance.
Dialogue: 0,2:01:36.54,2:01:38.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一并讨还所有的债\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Bringing it all.
Dialogue: 0,2:01:47.26,2:01:50.05,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}由我来说 我们可不想让人认出你\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'll talk. We don't want people realizing who you are.
Dialogue: 0,2:01:50.14,2:01:52.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那也许就不该带卫兵\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, maybe we shouldn't have brought a guard.
Dialogue: 0,2:01:52.81,2:01:54.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}路上真有麻烦 你就庆幸带了他们\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We'll be glad we did if we have trouble on the road.
Dialogue: 0,2:02:06.49,2:02:07.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}退后！ 让开！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Get back! Move!
Dialogue: 0,2:02:07.65,2:02:09.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我有口信 等等！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I have a message. Wait!
Dialogue: 0,2:02:11.45,2:02:12.49,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}欧迈俄斯派我来的！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Eumaeus sent me!
Dialogue: 0,2:02:14.70,2:02:15.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}把那个乞弓找来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Find that beggar.
Dialogue: 0,2:02:32.14,2:02:34.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你的人得在外面等 武器也要留下\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Your men must wait out here. The weapons too.
Dialogue: 0,2:02:51.49,2:02:53.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}陌生人 宙斯欢迎你们\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Zeus welcomes you, strangers.
Dialogue: 0,2:02:53.91,2:02:55.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们远道而来？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Have you traveled far?
Dialogue: 0,2:02:55.74,2:02:56.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不算远\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Not that far.
Dialogue: 0,2:02:58.12,2:03:00.04,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们是来借宿的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You're here to rest for the night.
Dialogue: 0,2:03:02.12,2:03:04.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们来向雅典娜献祭\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We're here to make sacrifice to Athena.
Dialogue: 0,2:03:06.55,2:03:09.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}至于你们的款待 倒也可以考虑\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And whatever hospitality you can offer might be considered.
Dialogue: 0,2:03:09.59,2:03:11.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}当然 把那个乞弓赶出去\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Of course. Get that beggar out of here.
Dialogue: 0,2:03:11.88,2:03:13.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他有口信带给我\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He has a message for me.
Dialogue: 0,2:03:14.60,2:03:15.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}欧迈俄斯派你来的？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Eumaeus sent you?
Dialogue: 0,2:03:16.97,2:03:18.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是的 大人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,2:03:23.94,2:03:25.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}什么口信？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, what's the message?
Dialogue: 0,2:03:26.61,2:03:28.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}得私下说\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's private.
Dialogue: 0,2:03:28.15,2:03:29.74,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这些人是\N{\rEN\blur0.8}These men are...
Dialogue: 0,2:03:30.70,2:03:31.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这些人是祭司\N{\rEN\blur0.8}These men are priests.
Dialogue: 0,2:03:49.42,2:03:51.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}老头 现在走还来得及\N{\rEN\blur0.8}This is your moment to leave, old man.
Dialogue: 0,2:03:51.88,2:03:53.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}走吧 陌生人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Go, stranger.
Dialogue: 0,2:03:56.14,2:03:58.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这星期我已经饶过一个老头\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I already spared one old man this week.
Dialogue: 0,2:03:58.81,2:03:59.97,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不过他是瞎子\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But he was blind.
Dialogue: 0,2:04:00.06,2:04:01.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我可不会再饶\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I won't spare...
Dialogue: 0,2:04:40.52,2:04:42.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一个乞弓 有这身手倒不错\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Not bad for a beggar.
Dialogue: 0,2:04:42.52,2:04:44.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没人天生就是乞弓\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No one's born a beggar.
Dialogue: 0,2:04:44.52,2:04:47.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}拿这些祭司袍 披在你们的盔甲上\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We'll take these priest robes, put 'em over your armor.
Dialogue: 0,2:04:49.82,2:04:52.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一帮我抬他的遗体 一我们必须留下他\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Help me with his body. We have to leave him.
Dialogue: 0,2:04:52.48,2:04:55.03,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一不行 一我们得悄悄溜出去\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-No. We have to slip out.
Dialogue: 0,2:04:55.11,2:04:57.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一这不是敬重死者的做法 一却能让你活命\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-That's not how you honor the dead. That is how you stay alive.
Dialogue: 0,2:04:57.91,2:04:59.49,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他是我的老师\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He was my teacher.
Dialogue: 0,2:05:00.58,2:05:01.74,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也许是雅典娜化身而来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He might have been Athena in disguise.
Dialogue: 0,2:05:01.83,2:05:03.33,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他叫门托尔\N{\rEN\blur0.8}His name was Mentor.
Dialogue: 0,2:05:04.08,2:05:05.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}等你安全了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And when you are safe,
Dialogue: 0,2:05:05.21,2:05:08.42,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们会去未知的西方 祭奠他\N{\rEN\blur0.8}we'll travel to the unknown west and we will honor him.
Dialogue: 0,2:05:09.08,2:05:11.04,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这些人是求婚者派来的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}These men were sent by the suitors.
Dialogue: 0,2:05:11.13,2:05:13.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还会有人来 我们得上路\N{\rEN\blur0.8}There will be more of them. We need to get on the road.
Dialogue: 0,2:05:13.55,2:05:15.55,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一摸黑走？ 一总比留在这里安全\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-By night? Safer than staying here.
Dialogue: 0,2:05:15.63,2:05:18.39,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}门托尔安卧在雅典娜最古老的神庙里\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Mentor's at the heart of Athena's oldest temple.
Dialogue: 0,2:05:19.01,2:05:21.14,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}此刻 就用火焰祭奠他吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}For now, we'll honor him in flame.
Dialogue: 0,2:05:30.90,2:05:32.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}着火了！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Fire!
Dialogue: 0,2:05:36.49,2:05:38.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}着火了！ 着火了！ 着着火了！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Fire! Fire! Fire!
Dialogue: 0,2:05:38.49,2:05:39.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}着火了！ 着火了！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Fire! Fire!
Dialogue: 0,2:06:00.09,2:06:02.01,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一个乞弓 怎么会认识门托尔？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}So how does a beggar come to know Mentor?
Dialogue: 0,2:06:02.10,2:06:04.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}说过了 我不是一直当乞\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I told you. I wasn't always a beggar.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:04.77,2:06:06.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你有一双睿智的眼睛\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You have wise eyes.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:07.27,2:06:09.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一像雅典娜的眼睛 一别在凡人中寻找神\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Athena's eyes.   -Don't look for gods in men.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:09.85,2:06:11.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你只会失望\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You'll just be disappointed.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:11.69,2:06:13.32,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那就告诉我 你是谁\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, then tell me who you are.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:14.90,2:06:16.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我叫西农\N{\rEN\blur0.8}My name is Sinon.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:16.90,2:06:20.11,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是个老兵 曾随你父亲在特洛伊作战\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm an old soldier who fought under your father at Troy.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:21.12,2:06:22.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你认识我父亲？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You knew my father?
Dialogue: 0,2:06:22.74,2:06:25.33,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}听他号令的年头 我都懒得数了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I've been taking orders from him for longer than I care to remember.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:26.83,2:06:28.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}等等 他还活着？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Wait, he's alive?
Dialogue: 0,2:06:29.12,2:06:30.17,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他活着\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He's alive.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:31.50,2:06:32.79,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他在哪儿？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, where is he?
Dialogue: 0,2:06:33.29,2:06:34.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就在附近\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He's close by.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:35.25,2:06:37.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他派我先来探探情形\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He sent me ahead to assess the situation.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:39.01,2:06:40.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}母亲一定不敢相信\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, Mother's not gonna believe it.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:40.80,2:06:42.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不 你不能告诉她\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No, you can't tell her.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:43.35,2:06:44.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}什么？ 一句也不说？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What, nothing?
Dialogue: 0,2:06:45.60,2:06:46.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}告诉她\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Tell her...
Dialogue: 0,2:06:47.81,2:06:50.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}告诉她 你认为她该改嫁了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Tell her you decided it's time she remarried.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:52.06,2:06:53.31,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他不必试探我母亲\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He doesn't need to test my mother.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:53.40,2:06:54.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他怎么能怀疑她？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}How could he doubt her?
Dialogue: 0,2:06:54.61,2:06:56.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他没有\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He doesn''t.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:56.15,2:06:58.53,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}但她有充分的理由忘记他\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But she has every reason to have forgotten him.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:00.36,2:07:01.95,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还有忠心的仆人吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Are there any loyal servants?
Dialogue: 0,2:07:02.99,2:07:04.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}有一些\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Some.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:04.95,2:07:06.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}奥德修斯一现身 就全都是了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}When Odysseus shows himself, all.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:08.45,2:07:10.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}得把求婚者都召集到王宫\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We need to gather the suitors at the palace.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:11.42,2:07:13.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这从来不成问题\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's never a problem.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:13.33,2:07:15.29,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}墨涅拉俄斯送你礼物了吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You have gifts from Menelaus?
Dialogue: 0,2:07:15.38,2:07:17.67,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一送了 在我的船上 一好\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Yeah, on my ship.   -Good.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:18.46,2:07:19.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}拿出王子的气派回去\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Come back as a prince.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:20.09,2:07:21.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}设一场宴席\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Call a banquet.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:21.80,2:07:22.93,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我会到场\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'll be there.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:23.93,2:07:25.39,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你在宴会上要做什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What will you do at the banquet?
Dialogue: 0,2:07:26.01,2:07:27.47,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}乞讨\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Beg.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:27.56,2:07:29.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}从低处 才最看得清一个人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The clearest view of a man is from below.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:31.64,2:07:33.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}求婚者有多少人？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}How many suitors are there?
Dialogue: 0,2:07:33.60,2:07:34.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}几十个\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Dozens.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:35.52,2:07:36.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不过 要是他的人个个都像你……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But if all of his men are like you, then...
Dialogue: 0,2:07:37.07,2:07:38.53,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他手下已经没人了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He doesn't have any men.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:39.40,2:07:40.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}什么 就你一个？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What, it's just you?
Dialogue: 0,2:07:41.86,2:07:42.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还有你\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And you.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:48.91,2:07:50.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}忒勒马科斯回来了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Telemachus is back.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:50.20,2:07:51.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-什么？  -忒勒马科斯回来了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-What?   -Telemachus is back.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:52.66,2:07:55.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-谁说的？  -大家都在说\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Who's saying this?   -Everyone's saying it.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:55.21,2:07:56.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}忒勒马科斯在哪儿？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Where's Telemachus?
Dialogue: 0,2:07:57.25,2:07:59.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}王后 您的位置不是在上面吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}My Queen! Surely your place is up there?
Dialogue: 0,2:08:08.01,2:08:09.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是真的？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's true?
Dialogue: 0,2:08:12.06,2:08:13.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你回来了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You're home.
Dialogue: 0,2:08:14.02,2:08:15.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我回来了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm back.
Dialogue: 0,2:08:15.69,2:08:17.15,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我想今晚我们可以庆祝一下\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I thought tonight we could celebrate.
Dialogue: 0,2:08:17.23,2:08:18.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}嗯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Hmm...
Dialogue: 0,2:08:18.32,2:08:21.03,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}要是还有东西能拿来庆祝的话\N{\rEN\blur0.8}If we have anything left to celebrate with.
Dialogue: 0,2:08:22.57,2:08:24.03,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}别担心\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Don't worry.
Dialogue: 0,2:08:24.11,2:08:26.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}英勇的求婚者们 自会厚礼相赠 庆庆贺你归来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}My brave suitors will shower us with gifts to honor your return.
Dialogue: 0,2:08:27.28,2:08:28.95,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}真高兴你平安归来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}So glad to see your safe return.
Dialogue: 0,2:08:39.84,2:08:41.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}真高兴你又能走动了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Glad to see you on your feet.
Dialogue: 0,2:08:42.09,2:08:43.97,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也该接你回王宫了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's about time we took you back to the palace.
Dialogue: 0,2:08:47.64,2:08:49.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}打听到你父亲的消息了吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What did you hear about your father?
Dialogue: 0,2:08:51.02,2:08:52.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没有\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Nothing.
Dialogue: 0,2:08:52.85,2:08:53.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}只有战争中的故事\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Stories from the war,
Dialogue: 0,2:08:54.02,2:08:56.27,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没人知道他离开特洛伊之后去了哪里\N{\rEN\blur0.8}but no one knew what happened to him after he left Troy.
Dialogue: 0,2:08:57.02,2:08:58.15,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}对不起 妈妈\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm sorry, Mom.
Dialogue: 0,2:08:59.06,2:09:02.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}斯巴达人都在谈论一场即将来临的浩劫\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Everyone in Sparta is talking about a coming catastrophe.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:03.61,2:09:07.45,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}海上来的人践踏宙斯律法 将带来黑暗时代\N{\rEN\blur0.8}An age of darkness brought on by people from the sea violating Zeus' Law.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:07.53,2:09:08.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这么说 传闻是真的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}So the stories are true.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:08.99,2:09:10.95,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们的文明正在崩塌\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Our civilization is collapsing.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:11.45,2:09:13.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}墨涅拉俄斯担心 我们召集不起军队\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Menelaus is concerned that we can't raise an army
Dialogue: 0,2:09:13.16,2:09:14.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}因为王位空悬\N{\rEN\blur0.8}with an empty throne.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:14.58,2:09:16.04,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}所以我们想了个办法\N{\rEN\blur0.8}So we came up with a plan.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:17.67,2:09:18.67,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}什么办法？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What plan?
Dialogue: 0,2:09:20.84,2:09:22.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}唯一能让求婚者离开的办法\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The one way to get the suitors to leave.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:25.22,2:09:26.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你该做出选择了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's time for you to choose.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:30.60,2:09:32.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你想让我改嫁？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You want me to remarry?
Dialogue: 0,2:09:32.26,2:09:35.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}只要你改嫁 其他求婚者就会走\N{\rEN\blur0.8}If you remarry, the other suitors will leave.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:35.10,2:09:37.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我就只需要对付一个人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And then I'm only dealing with one of them.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:37.10,2:09:38.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我快成年了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm almost of age.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:38.19,2:09:41.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我会告诉长老们 在斯巴达得知了奥德修斯的死讯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'll tell the elders that I learned of Odysseus' death in Sparta.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:42.15,2:09:45.15,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}墨涅拉俄斯会替我作证 他们就会让我继位\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Menelaus will back me up, and they'll let me assume the throne.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:45.24,2:09:47.36,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你背弃父亲 我离开自己的家\N{\rEN\blur0.8}So you deny your father, and I leave my home
Dialogue: 0,2:09:47.45,2:09:48.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}去和这些毒蛇中的一条过日子\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and go live with one of these snakes.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:48.86,2:09:49.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这就是你的办法\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's your plan.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:49.95,2:09:51.49,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那你有更好的办法吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, do you have a better one?
Dialogue: 0,2:09:54.16,2:09:57.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}锁上门 放把火 烧死这群混蛋\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Lock the door, set a fire, and burn the bastards.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:58.62,2:10:02.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你以为我改嫁 日子就能回到从前？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Do you think if I remarry life goes back to the way it was?
Dialogue: 0,2:10:03.30,2:10:05.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}从前的世界已经没了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That world is gone.
Dialogue: 0,2:10:05.34,2:10:06.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}如今这个世界\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And, in this one,
Dialogue: 0,2:10:06.46,2:10:08.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们不会把权力交给你\N{\rEN\blur0.8}they're not giving up power to you.
Dialogue: 0,2:10:08.51,2:10:09.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也不会交给奥德修斯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Or Odysseus.
Dialogue: 0,2:10:09.59,2:10:11.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他若回来 也得杀了他们\N{\rEN\blur0.8}If he returned, he'd have to kill them.
Dialogue: 0,2:10:12.30,2:10:13.47,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就像你要做的一样\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Like you will.
Dialogue: 0,2:10:14.18,2:10:17.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}杀了他们 他们的家人就会要求复仇\N{\rEN\blur0.8}If I kill them, their families will demand revenge.
Dialogue: 0,2:10:17.18,2:10:18.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我会被流放\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'd be exiled.
Dialogue: 0,2:10:19.48,2:10:21.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没有我 王位就会落入他人之手\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And, without me, the throne'll be lost.
Dialogue: 0,2:10:21.19,2:10:22.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}因为只有男人才能坐上去\N{\rEN\blur0.8}'Cause only a man can sit on it.
Dialogue: 0,2:10:24.73,2:10:25.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}王位空悬？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Empty throne?
Dialogue: 0,2:10:27.70,2:10:31.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我在那空悬的王位上 已经坐了二十年！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I've been sitting on that empty throne for 20 years!
Dialogue: 0,2:10:31.28,2:10:33.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我的学识 多多年的经验\N{\rEN\blur0.8}My knowledge, my years of experience
Dialogue: 0,2:10:33.99,2:10:36.75,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}竞都比不上你下巴上那几根胡子\N{\rEN\blur0.8}that's all nothing compared to the bristles on your chin.
Dialogue: 0,2:10:39.58,2:10:40.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你想要和平？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Do you want peace?
Dialogue: 0,2:10:42.00,2:10:43.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-还是复仇？  -我要奥德修斯！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Or do you want revenge?   -I want Odysseus!
Dialogue: 0,2:10:47.30,2:10:48.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}歌唱吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Sing...
Dialogue: 0,2:10:49.05,2:10:50.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}缪斯啊 唱那一张面孔\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Muse, of a face...
Dialogue: 0,2:10:53.85,2:10:55.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一张面孔\N{\rEN\blur0.8}...a face...
Dialogue: 0,2:10:59.39,2:11:00.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}支舰队·\N{\rEN\blur0.8}...a fleet...
Dialogue: 0,2:11:04.82,2:11:05.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一场战争……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}...a war...
Dialogue: 0,2:11:10.20,2:11:11.36,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}在特洛伊.·\N{\rEN\blur0.8}...at Troy...
Dialogue: 0,2:11:15.41,2:11:17.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}歌唱吧 缪斯 唱那个男人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Sing, Muse, of a man...
Dialogue: 0,2:11:21.66,2:11:22.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一个男人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}...@2 man...
Dialogue: 0,2:11:26.96,2:11:28.05,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一个念头■\N{\rEN\blur0.8}...a thought...
Dialogue: 0,2:11:32.05,2:11:33.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}小条计策·\N{\rEN\blur0.8}...@2 fick...
Dialogue: 0,2:11:36.97,2:11:38.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}欧迈俄斯 你先走\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Eumaeus, go ahead.
Dialogue: 0,2:11:45.02,2:11:46.27,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}阿尔戈斯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Argus.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:09.17,2:12:11.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}把它葬在悬崖上吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You should bury him up on the cliff.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:13.18,2:12:14.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们相遇的地方？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Where you met?
Dialogue: 0,2:12:23.10,2:12:24.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你是奥德修斯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You're Odysseus.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:27.52,2:12:29.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你是我的父亲\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You're my father.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:31.61,2:12:32.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是个乞\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm a beggar.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:36.20,2:12:37.32,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}而你\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And you
Dialogue: 0,2:12:39.37,2:12:40.74,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是个优秀的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}are the worthy,
Dialogue: 0,2:12:42.08,2:12:45.04,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}俊美的奥德修斯之子\N{\rEN\blur0.8}beautiful son of Odysseus.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:46.71,2:12:49.96,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}等你们终于相见时\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Of whom, when you do finally meet,
Dialogue: 0,2:12:52.05,2:12:53.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他一定会以你为荣\N{\rEN\blur0.8}he will be so proud.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:57.55,2:13:00.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}欢迎回家 陌生人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Welcome home, stranger.
Dialogue: 0,2:13:03.64,2:13:05.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}因为胜利的阴影\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Because the darkness of victory
Dialogue: 0,2:13:06.52,2:13:08.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}笼罩了谱写传奇的人·\N{\rEN\blur0.8}shrouds the writers of legends...
Dialogue: 0,2:13:10.73,2:13:13.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-让我们全都成了吟游诗人和盲眼乞弓\N{\rEN\blur0.8}...and make bards and blind beggars of us all.
Dialogue: 0,2:13:20.78,2:13:22.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}请接受宙斯的款待\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Accept the hospitality of Zeus.
Dialogue: 0,2:13:23.37,2:13:25.21,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}给这位陌生人拿些吃的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Get the stranger some food.
Dialogue: 0,2:13:25.29,2:13:26.29,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不必了 大人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No, sir.
Dialogue: 0,2:13:27.12,2:13:29.17,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我端个碗 四处讨一点就好\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'll just make the rounds with a bowl.
Dialogue: 0,2:13:34.59,2:13:37.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}怎么又请了个舔盘子的脏鬼来吃饭？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Had to invite another one of these filthy plate-lickers to dinner?
Dialogue: 0,2:13:37.30,2:13:39.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这场盛宴 多一个乞弓又何妨？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What's one more beggar at this feast?
Dialogue: 0,2:13:57.32,2:13:59.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}得在他重新获得长老支持前 杀了他\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We need to kill him before he regains his position with the elders.
Dialogue: 0,2:13:59.91,2:14:01.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}怎么杀？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}How?
Dialogue: 0,2:14:16.46,2:14:17.47,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}拿酒来！ 快拿来！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Bring the wine! Bring it!
Dialogue: 0,2:14:17.55,2:14:19.01,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}激怒他\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Provoke him.
Dialogue: 0,2:14:19.59,2:14:21.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}引他拿起武器\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Get him to grab one of the weapons.
Dialogue: 0,2:14:25.68,2:14:28.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他已不是当年那个一逗就跳的小崽子\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He's not the same young pup we used to bait.
Dialogue: 0,2:14:28.56,2:14:30.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那今晚回来 割断他的喉咙\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Then we come back tonight, and we cut his throat.
Dialogue: 0,2:14:32.52,2:14:34.15,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一滚开 老头 一求求你\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Fuck off, old man. Please.
Dialogue: 0,2:14:34.98,2:14:36.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我好几天没吃东西了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's been days since I've eaten.
Dialogue: 0,2:14:36.36,2:14:37.36,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我他妈叫你滚！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I told you to fuck off!
Dialogue: 0,2:14:37.44,2:14:41.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}吃的又不是你的 慷慨一点也不行？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You can't be generous with food that's not even yours?
Dialogue: 0,2:14:42.74,2:14:44.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你的碗都装满了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}There's no room in your bowl.
Dialogue: 0,2:14:44.20,2:14:45.45,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还装得下\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yes, there is.
Dialogue: 0,2:14:47.08,2:14:48.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}嗯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Hmm...
Dialogue: 0,2:14:50.67,2:14:52.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还真是\N{\rEN\blur0.8}So there is.
Dialogue: 0,2:14:53.96,2:14:55.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}给你\N{\rEN\blur0.8}There you go.
Dialogue: 0,2:14:59.30,2:15:00.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}现在该来找我要东西了吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Suppose you want something from me now.
Dialogue: 0,2:15:00.97,2:15:02.01,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No.
Dialogue: 0,2:15:02.64,2:15:04.39,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我有东西要给你\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I have something for you.
Dialogue: 0,2:15:05.35,2:15:07.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你有东西给我？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You have something for me?
Dialogue: 0,2:15:07.81,2:15:09.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他有东西要给我！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He has something for me!
Dialogue: 0,2:15:11.23,2:15:14.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你这种又老又脏的舔盘鬼\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What could a filthy old plate-licker like you
Dialogue: 0,2:15:14.77,2:15:17.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}能有什么东西让我想要？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}possibly have that I could want?
Dialogue: 0,2:15:17.69,2:15:20.36,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}其实 这本来就是你的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Actually, it's yours.
Dialogue: 0,2:15:25.74,2:15:27.49,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}有人托我归还\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I was asked to return it.
Dialogue: 0,2:15:29.62,2:15:30.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不是我的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's not mine.
Dialogue: 0,2:15:32.54,2:15:33.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不是吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No?
Dialogue: 0,2:15:36.92,2:15:38.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你从哪儿弄来的？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Where did you get this?
Dialogue: 0,2:15:40.51,2:15:42.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不许背对着我！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Don't turn your back on me!
Dialogue: 0,2:15:47.85,2:15:50.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}安提诺俄斯 不能这样对待乞弓\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Antinous, you can't treat a beggar like that.
Dialogue: 0,2:15:50.98,2:15:52.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这是宙斯的律法\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's Zeus' Law.
Dialogue: 0,2:15:52.60,2:15:53.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}宙斯的律法\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Zeus' Law.
Dialogue: 0,2:15:58.40,2:15:59.74,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你觉得这是位神？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You think this is a god?
Dialogue: 0,2:16:03.32,2:16:05.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}觉得他是神明化身？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Think this is a god in disguise?
Dialogue: 0,2:16:06.03,2:16:07.03,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你是吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Are you?
Dialogue: 0,2:16:08.83,2:16:10.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你是神吗\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Are you a god,
Dialogue: 0,2:16:11.20,2:16:12.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}舔盘鬼？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}plate-licker?
Dialogue: 0,2:16:13.42,2:16:14.42,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不是\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No.
Dialogue: 0,2:16:15.17,2:16:17.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是参加过特洛伊战争的老兵\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm a veteran of the Trojan War.
Dialogue: 0,2:16:17.34,2:16:19.96,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}特洛伊战争的老兵\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Veteran of the Trojan War.
Dialogue: 0,2:16:22.55,2:16:24.05,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那你叫什么 老兵？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And what's your name, veteran?
Dialogue: 0,2:16:28.30,2:16:29.31,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}西农\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Sinon.
Dialogue: 0,2:16:32.98,2:16:34.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这个名字 对你有什么意义吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Does that name mean something to you?
Dialogue: 0,2:16:35.60,2:16:36.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没有\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No.
Dialogue: 0,2:16:37.69,2:16:41.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我用它纪念我见过最勇敢的年轻人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I use it to honor the bravest young man I ever met.
Dialogue: 0,2:16:42.44,2:16:43.53,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}西农\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Sinon.
Dialogue: 0,2:16:45.16,2:16:46.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那不是你家牧羊人的儿子吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Wasn't that your shepherd's boy?
Dialogue: 0,2:16:49.37,2:16:50.45,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我不记得了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't remember that.
Dialogue: 0,2:16:50.54,2:16:53.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}对 对 他当时想让你顶替他\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yeah, yeah, he wanted you to take his place.
Dialogue: 0,2:16:53.66,2:16:55.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你在哪儿找到的？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Where did you find this?
Dialogue: 0,2:16:55.50,2:16:56.83,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你很快就要去的地方\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Where you'll soon be.
Dialogue: 0,2:16:57.83,2:16:58.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}什么地方？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And where is that?
Dialogue: 0,2:16:59.54,2:17:00.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}冥府\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Hades.
Dialogue: 0,2:17:04.34,2:17:05.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}够了！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Enough!
Dialogue: 0,2:17:07.14,2:17:08.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}宴席结束！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The feast is done!
Dialogue: 0,2:17:13.14,2:17:14.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}走吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,2:17:15.31,2:17:16.73,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不是我的！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's not mine!
Dialogue: 0,2:17:25.57,2:17:27.53,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}王后想和你谈谈\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The Queen would like to speak with you.
Dialogue: 0,2:17:27.61,2:17:30.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}留下等众人离开 炉火点起\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Stay till everyone's left and the fires are lit.
Dialogue: 0,2:18:21.00,2:18:22.29,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你好 旅人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Hello, traveler.
Dialogue: 0,2:18:23.42,2:18:24.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}王后\N{\rEN\blur0.8}My Queen.
Dialogue: 0,2:18:24.80,2:18:28.67,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}墨兰托 让欧律克勒娅替客人洗脚\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Melantho, have Eurycleia wash the stranger's feet.
Dialogue: 0,2:18:28.76,2:18:30.09,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不必了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's not necessary.
Dialogue: 0,2:18:30.18,2:18:33.76,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我丈夫坚持 要把客人当家人一样敬重\N{\rEN\blur0.8}My husband insisted we honor guests as family.
Dialogue: 0,2:18:34.39,2:18:36.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你听说过我的丈夫奥德修斯吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You know of Odysseus, my husband?
Dialogue: 0,2:18:36.85,2:18:37.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}当然\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Of course.
Dialogue: 0,2:18:38.39,2:18:39.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}从歌谣里？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Through the songs.
Dialogue: 0,2:18:40.23,2:18:41.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我去过特洛伊 夫人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I was at Troy, ma'am.
Dialogue: 0,2:18:42.48,2:18:44.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那么那些歌谣 你听着大概很可笑\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Then the songs probably seem silly.
Dialogue: 0,2:18:45.98,2:18:47.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}它们让我落泪\N{\rEN\blur0.8}They make me cry.
Dialogue: 0,2:18:48.44,2:18:49.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}为什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Why?
Dialogue: 0,2:18:49.70,2:18:51.53,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}为了失去的一切\N{\rEN\blur0.8}For what was lost.
Dialogue: 0,2:18:52.41,2:18:53.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那些生命？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The lives?
Dialogue: 0,2:18:54.24,2:18:55.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还有那些岁月\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And the years.
Dialogue: 0,2:18:56.70,2:18:57.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}所有的一切\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Everything.
Dialogue: 0,2:19:05.34,2:19:07.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你在特洛伊认识奥德修斯吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Did you know Odysseus at Troy?
Dialogue: 0,2:19:07.59,2:19:08.76,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}认识\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I did.
Dialogue: 0,2:19:10.01,2:19:13.93,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他穿什么 戴什么 你还记得什么细节吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Was there some detail of how he dressed, something he wore?
Dialogue: 0,2:19:14.64,2:19:16.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他戴着一枚奇特的别针\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He wore a strange pin.
Dialogue: 0,2:19:16.68,2:19:18.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}奇特？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Strange?
Dialogue: 0,2:19:18.77,2:19:19.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}很美\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Beautiful.
Dialogue: 0,2:19:20.64,2:19:21.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}却格格不入\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But out of place.
Dialogue: 0,2:19:22.35,2:19:23.36,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}说说它的样子\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Describe it.
Dialogue: 0,2:19:37.87,2:19:39.45,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我再去取些水\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'll get more water.
Dialogue: 0,2:19:43.75,2:19:46.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那是一枚精美的金别针\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It was a beautiful, gold pin.
Dialogue: 0,2:19:47.75,2:19:50.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}雅典娜的身像 周围环绕着藤蔓\N{\rEN\blur0.8}A figure of Athena encircled by vines.
Dialogue: 0,2:19:59.31,2:20:00.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他常戴着吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Did he wear it often?
Dialogue: 0,2:20:02.27,2:20:03.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}从没摘下来过\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He never took it off.
Dialogue: 0,2:20:23.92,2:20:26.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}为什么你回来了 奥德修斯却回不来？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}How is it that you made it home when Odysseus could not?
Dialogue: 0,2:20:27.88,2:20:30.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我还没回家 还没有\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm not home. Not yet.
Dialogue: 0,2:20:31.46,2:20:32.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}为什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Why not?
Dialogue: 0,2:20:32.80,2:20:35.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}归家 并非总是易事\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's not always an easy thing, a homecoming.
Dialogue: 0,2:20:36.26,2:20:38.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}奥德修斯如此 我也一样\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's as true for Odysseus as for me.
Dialogue: 0,2:20:40.14,2:20:41.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我认识的奥德修斯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The Odysseus I knew,
Dialogue: 0,2:20:42.85,2:20:47.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不管怎样 都会想尽办法杀出一条归路\N{\rEN\blur0.8}would have found or fought his way back to me no matter what.
Dialogue: 0,2:20:48.52,2:20:51.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}如果你认识的奥德修斯迷失了呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What if the Odysseus you knew lost his way?
Dialogue: 0,2:20:56.45,2:20:59.83,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}如果在某个夜晚\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What if, one night,
Dialogue: 0,2:21:00.95,2:21:02.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一座陌生的城里\N{\rEN\blur0.8}in a strange city,
Dialogue: 0,2:21:04.21,2:21:05.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他看到了某些事\N{\rEN\blur0.8}he saw things
Dialogue: 0,2:21:06.96,2:21:09.42,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}让他觉得 熟悉的家园\N{\rEN\blur0.8}that made him think the home he knew
Dialogue: 0,2:21:10.75,2:21:12.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}已不可能还在原地等他呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}couldn't possibly be there anymore?
Dialogue: 0,2:21:16.84,2:21:17.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}如果\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What if,
Dialogue: 0,2:21:18.34,2:21:20.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他从木马腹中钻出来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}when he left the belly of the horse
Dialogue: 0,2:21:24.60,2:21:26.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}打开特洛伊城门时\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and opened the gates of Troy,
Dialogue: 0,2:21:31.90,2:21:34.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}看着积压十年的怒火\N{\rEN\blur0.8}he saw ten years of rage
Dialogue: 0,2:21:34.74,2:21:37.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}在一夜之间涌进城中呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}pour into that city in one night?
Dialogue: 0,2:22:25.04,2:22:27.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}所有人 动手！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Everyone, now!
Dialogue: 0,2:23:53.33,2:23:56.42,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们留给他们一份礼物\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We left them a gift.
Dialogue: 0,2:23:56.50,2:23:59.17,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一份和平的献礼\N{\rEN\blur0.8}An offering of peace.
Dialogue: 0,2:23:59.26,2:24:02.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们把它带进了家园\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That they took into their home.
Dialogue: 0,2:24:12.73,2:24:15.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们践踏了人与人之间\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We violated all that's ever sacred
Dialogue: 0,2:24:16.90,2:24:18.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一切神圣的准则\N{\rEN\blur0.8}between people.
Dialogue: 0,2:24:20.44,2:24:21.49,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}把一场战斗·\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And turned a fight...
Dialogue: 0,2:24:22.44,2:24:23.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}砸毁他们的神像！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Destroy their idols!
Dialogue: 0,2:24:25.45,2:24:26.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}变成了一场猎杀\N{\rEN\blur0.8}... into a hunt.
Dialogue: 0,2:24:31.04,2:24:32.04,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}求求你 不要\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Please don't.
Dialogue: 0,2:24:42.67,2:24:44.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}烧毁特洛伊的城墙\N{\rEN\blur0.8}7o burn the walls of Troy
Dialogue: 0,2:24:45.22,2:24:47.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就是烧毁整个世界\N{\rEN\blur0.8}was to burn the world entire.
Dialogue: 0,2:24:49.43,2:24:51.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}包括他自己的家\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Including his home.
Dialogue: 0,2:24:57.86,2:24:59.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}如果他明白\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What if he knew
Dialogue: 0,2:25:00.86,2:25:02.19,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就在那一夜\N{\rEN\blur0.8}that very night...
Dialogue: 0,2:25:05.36,2:25:09.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}穿过混乱与痛苦的烈火之时\N{\rEN\blur0.8}...@S he walked through fires of anarchy and pain...
Dialogue: 0,2:25:58.92,2:26:02.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}以及随后那些挥汗狂欢的日子里\N{\rEN\blur0.8}...and in the days of sweaty celebrations to follow...
Dialogue: 0,2:26:08.68,2:26:11.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}如果他清楚自己做下了什么呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}...What if he knew exactly what he'd done?
Dialogue: 0,2:26:30.53,2:26:32.33,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是你们所有人做下的事\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What all of you had done.
Dialogue: 0,2:26:32.41,2:26:34.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一个人的念头\N{\rEN\blur0.8}One man's idea.
Dialogue: 0,2:26:35.58,2:26:37.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一个人的计策\N{\rEN\blur0.8}One man's trick.
Dialogue: 0,2:26:38.71,2:26:41.42,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}永远打破了宙斯的律法\N{\rEN\blur0.8}To break Zeus' Law forever.
Dialogue: 0,2:26:42.79,2:26:45.96,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们曾生活在一个宫殿林立 商贸繁荣的世界\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We lived in a world of palaces and trade.
Dialogue: 0,2:26:47.63,2:26:48.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还有文字\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And language.
Dialogue: 0,2:26:48.88,2:26:50.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}却看不见它的美好\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Blind to its beauty.
Dialogue: 0,2:26:51.64,2:26:53.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}直到亲手毁了它\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Until we broke it.
Dialogue: 0,2:26:55.68,2:26:57.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们就是那些海上来的人？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You are the people from the sea?
Dialogue: 0,2:27:00.48,2:27:01.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是的 王后\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yes, my Queen.
Dialogue: 0,2:27:03.36,2:27:06.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}践踏宙斯律法的恶行 正像瘟疫般蔓延\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The breaking of Zeus' Law is spreading like plague.
Dialogue: 0,2:27:06.78,2:27:08.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们的青铜时代 正在崩塌\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Our age of bronze is collapsing.
Dialogue: 0,2:27:08.53,2:27:12.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也许他不忍再看自己造成的满目疮\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And maybe he couldn't bear to see the ruins of what he'd done.
Dialogue: 0,2:27:12.99,2:27:13.99,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}无论在什么地方\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Anywhere.
Dialogue: 0,2:27:14.53,2:27:16.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}尤其是自己的家\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Least of all, his home.
Dialogue: 0,2:27:26.17,2:27:27.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可奥德修斯还活着\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But Odysseus is alive.
Dialogue: 0,2:27:29.72,2:27:31.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}在你最需要他时 他会来到你身边\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And he'll be here when you need him most.
Dialogue: 0,2:27:34.01,2:27:35.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那么\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well,
Dialogue: 0,2:27:36.51,2:27:39.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我在他留下的废墟里 已经住得够久了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I've been living in his ruins long enough.
Dialogue: 0,2:27:44.61,2:27:46.11,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}黎明时 叫求婚者都来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Bring the suitors at dawn.
Dialogue: 0,2:27:46.19,2:27:48.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}把大厅里的武器都撤走\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Remove the arms from the hall.
Dialogue: 0,2:27:48.32,2:27:52.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}再过几小时 一人得意 其余人便会恼羞成恨\N{\rEN\blur0.8}In a few hours, one suitor will be happy and the rest angry, vengeful men.
Dialogue: 0,2:27:52.66,2:27:54.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}兵刃会勾起人的杀心\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Bronze draws a man on,
Dialogue: 0,2:27:54.20,2:27:57.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}所以比试时不得携带武器 大门也要锁上\N{\rEN\blur0.8}so we'll have no weapons at the trial and the doors will be locked.
Dialogue: 0,2:27:57.95,2:28:00.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}谁能完成我的考验 我就嫁给谁\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'll marry whoever completes my challenge.
Dialogue: 0,2:28:06.92,2:28:08.55,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们要怎么对付求婚者？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}How will we take on the suitors?
Dialogue: 0,2:28:09.51,2:28:10.76,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不是我们\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Not "we."
Dialogue: 0,2:28:11.30,2:28:13.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们的血 应该沾在我手上\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Their blood belongs on my hands.
Dialogue: 0,2:28:13.84,2:28:15.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}否则你就得被流放\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Or you face exile.
Dialogue: 0,2:28:16.30,2:28:17.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你就不会吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Won't you?
Dialogue: 0,2:28:18.35,2:28:20.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}只管确保他们拿不到武器\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Just make sure they can't get those weapons.
Dialogue: 0,2:28:20.77,2:28:21.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我会办好\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'll see to it.
Dialogue: 0,2:28:22.73,2:28:24.73,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们就算手无寸铁 人也太多了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Even unarmed, there are so many of them.
Dialogue: 0,2:28:25.52,2:28:27.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你也不会有武器\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And you won't have a weapon.
Dialogue: 0,2:28:28.52,2:28:29.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我会有武器的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, I'll have a weapon.
Dialogue: 0,2:28:31.69,2:28:33.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你母亲已经安排好了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Your mother's seen to that.
Dialogue: 0,2:28:35.66,2:28:37.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}把你信任的仆人召集起来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Gather the servants you trust.
Dialogue: 0,2:28:37.99,2:28:39.83,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}将武器锁进楼上的储藏室\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Lock the arms in the upper storage room.
Dialogue: 0,2:28:39.91,2:28:41.04,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好 我会办妥\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yes, I'll see to it.
Dialogue: 0,2:28:59.22,2:29:01.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}快 快 把武器搬到楼上\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Hurry, hurry. Get the weapons upstairs.
Dialogue: 0,2:29:09.19,2:29:10.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}快点 快点\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Hurry, hurry.
Dialogue: 0,2:29:33.09,2:29:35.05,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}看来宙斯也想知道结果\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Zeus seems interested in the outcome.
Dialogue: 0,2:29:35.13,2:29:36.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可到底比试什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But what's the trial?
Dialogue: 0,2:30:00.99,2:30:02.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这些年来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}For years,
Dialogue: 0,2:30:03.54,2:30:05.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我丈夫不在家\N{\rEN\blur0.8}while my husband's been gone,
Dialogue: 0,2:30:05.91,2:30:08.75,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们便霸占王宫 大摆筵席\N{\rEN\blur0.8}you've commandeered this palace for your feasting.
Dialogue: 0,2:30:09.42,2:30:12.63,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}借口是想赢得我的芳心 娶我为妻\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Your excuse was you wanted to win my hand in marriage.
Dialogue: 0,2:30:16.26,2:30:20.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我听着你们寻欢作乐 争斗不休\N{\rEN\blur0.8}As I listened to you party and fight,
Dialogue: 0,2:30:22.51,2:30:26.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}带坏我的仆人 作践我的家园\N{\rEN\blur0.8}corrupt my servants and disrespect my home,
Dialogue: 0,2:30:26.94,2:30:29.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}只盼奥德修斯归来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I've wanted nothing more than for Odysseus to return
Dialogue: 0,2:30:29.31,2:30:31.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}亲眼看看这一切\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and see all this for himself.
Dialogue: 0,2:30:37.99,2:30:40.95,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}但昨夜 我终于明白\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But, last night, I realized
Dialogue: 0,2:30:41.03,2:30:42.33,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他此刻不在这里\N{\rEN\blur0.8}he's not here now.
Dialogue: 0,2:30:46.08,2:30:47.29,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}以后也不会再回来了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He never will be.
Dialogue: 0,2:30:49.25,2:30:50.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}所以\N{\rEN\blur0.8}So,
Dialogue: 0,2:30:51.17,2:30:54.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}在场任何人 只要能做到 我便愿意嫁给他\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I stand ready to marry anyone here
Dialogue: 0,2:30:54.46,2:30:59.76,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}给这张猎弓上弦 再一箭穿过那十二柄斧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}who can string this hunting bow and shoot an arrow through those 12 axes.
Dialogue: 0,2:31:01.55,2:31:03.05,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}上前来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Step up.
Dialogue: 0,2:31:04.89,2:31:06.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}让我看看你们究竟是谁\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And show me who you are.
Dialogue: 0,2:31:07.81,2:31:08.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}欧迈俄斯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Eumaeus.
Dialogue: 0,2:31:20.57,2:31:22.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}谁先来？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Who's first?
Dialogue: 0,2:31:22.16,2:31:23.24,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}把弓给我\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Give me the bow.
Dialogue: 0,2:31:43.93,2:31:44.97,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}根本做不到\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It can't be done.
Dialogue: 0,2:31:45.05,2:31:46.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是你做不到\N{\rEN\blur0.8}By you.
Dialogue: 0,2:31:46.51,2:31:48.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我小时候 见过奥德修斯轻松做到\N{\rEN\blur0.8}As a boy, I saw Odysseus do it with ease.
Dialogue: 0,2:31:48.77,2:31:49.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那你来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Then you do it.
Dialogue: 0,2:31:50.77,2:31:51.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我会等轮到我\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'll wait my turn.
Dialogue: 0,2:31:53.06,2:31:55.32,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}何不把弓烤热 再抹些油？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Why don't we warm the bow and oil it?
Dialogue: 0,2:31:56.77,2:31:58.74,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这张弓多年没上过弦了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}This bow hasn't been strung in years.
Dialogue: 0,2:32:32.23,2:32:33.27,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}轮到你了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Your turn.
Dialogue: 0,2:32:33.35,2:32:34.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没必要\N{\rEN\blur0.8}There's no need.
Dialogue: 0,2:32:37.98,2:32:39.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}王后的意思 已经很明白了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}My Queen has made her point.
Dialogue: 0,2:32:39.57,2:32:41.53,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们谁也代替不了奥德修斯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We can't replace Odysseus.
Dialogue: 0,2:32:41.61,2:32:43.24,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}有些人一直都知道这一点\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Some of us have always known that.
Dialogue: 0,2:32:43.32,2:32:46.24,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}有些人本愿随那位英雄征战特洛伊\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Some of us would have followed that great man to Troy.
Dialogue: 0,2:32:46.32,2:32:47.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}只要他肯答应\N{\rEN\blur0.8}If he'd let us.
Dialogue: 0,2:32:50.20,2:32:51.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可他再也没回来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But he never came back.
Dialogue: 0,2:32:53.62,2:32:55.21,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}所以 从我们之中挑一个最好的吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}So choose the best of us here.
Dialogue: 0,2:32:56.88,2:32:59.21,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们都没通过你的考验\N{\rEN\blur0.8}All of us who've failed your test.
Dialogue: 0,2:32:59.80,2:33:00.96,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我还没有\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I haven't.
Dialogue: 0,2:33:05.84,2:33:07.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}来人 把这些乞弓赶出去！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Somebody get these beggars out of here!
Dialogue: 0,2:33:08.68,2:33:11.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}比试结束前 大门不得打开\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The doors are locked until the trial's over.
Dialogue: 0,2:33:11.68,2:33:14.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一比试已经结束了 一对\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-The trial is over. Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,2:33:14.31,2:33:15.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我想试试\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I wanna try.
Dialogue: 0,2:33:15.44,2:33:17.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}歇着吧 老头\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Give it a rest, old man.
Dialogue: 0,2:33:18.73,2:33:20.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不 他有权试试\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No, he has a right to try.
Dialogue: 0,2:33:21.78,2:33:23.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你既然不肯 就让他来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}If you won't, he may as well.
Dialogue: 0,2:33:24.40,2:33:26.36,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你是在拿母亲的心愿开玩笑\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You're making a mockery of your mother's wishes.
Dialogue: 0,2:33:26.45,2:33:28.87,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我母亲的心愿 是你们全被烧死\N{\rEN\blur0.8}My mother's wishes are for you all to burn.
Dialogue: 0,2:33:40.46,2:33:42.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他是个老弓手\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He's an old archer.
Dialogue: 0,2:33:45.97,2:33:47.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}来吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Come on.
Dialogue: 0,2:33:47.80,2:33:49.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}瞧瞧行家出手\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Look at the expert at work.
Dialogue: 0,2:33:49.97,2:33:52.01,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}舔盘鬼！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Plate-licker!
Dialogue: 0,2:33:52.81,2:33:53.93,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}来啊！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Come on!
Dialogue: 0,2:33:54.02,2:33:55.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}算了吧 老老头！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Old man, forget it!
Dialogue: 0,2:33:56.73,2:33:57.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}喂 老头！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Hey, old man!
Dialogue: 0,2:33:58.56,2:33:59.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}来啊！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Come on!
Dialogue: 0,2:34:07.11,2:34:08.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好了 朋友\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Okay, friend.
Dialogue: 0,2:34:08.78,2:34:09.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}朋友 够了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Friend, that's enough.
Dialogue: 0,2:34:09.99,2:34:11.24,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}让他试试\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Let him try.
Dialogue: 0,2:34:11.33,2:34:12.99,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一让他试试 一来吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Let him try. Come on.
Dialogue: 0,2:34:54.87,2:34:56.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你是奥德\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-You're Odyss...
Dialogue: 0,2:35:02.08,2:35:04.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你的位置 应该在下面吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Surely your place is down there.
Dialogue: 0,2:35:18.81,2:35:19.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是他吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Is it him?
Dialogue: 0,2:35:20.85,2:35:21.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是他\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's him.
Dialogue: 0,2:35:31.66,2:35:32.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}去守住武器\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Go secure the weapons.
Dialogue: 0,2:35:47.42,2:35:48.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}武器在哪儿？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Where are the weapons?
Dialogue: 0,2:35:48.92,2:35:49.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}楼上的储藏室\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The upper store room.
Dialogue: 0,2:35:50.01,2:35:51.01,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}去拿！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Get them!
Dialogue: 0,2:35:55.22,2:35:58.47,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还等什么？ 他要把我们全杀了！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What are you waiting for? He's gonna kill us all!
Dialogue: 0,2:36:01.94,2:36:03.19,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}小心！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Look out!
Dialogue: 0,2:36:08.40,2:36:10.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}说过了 牧牛的 你声音太大了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I told you. Too loud, cowherd.
Dialogue: 0,2:36:10.94,2:36:12.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不！ 不！ 不！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No! No! No!
Dialogue: 0,2:36:13.53,2:36:16.24,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}欧迈俄斯！ 放我出去！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Eumaeus! Let me out!
Dialogue: 0,2:36:21.58,2:36:22.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}趴下！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Down!
Dialogue: 0,2:36:33.43,2:36:34.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No!
Dialogue: 0,2:37:29.82,2:37:31.15,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}拿剑！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Get the swords!
Dialogue: 0,2:38:31.00,2:38:33.09,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}拿盾牌！ 拿盾牌！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Get the shields! Get the shields!
Dialogue: 0,2:39:12.08,2:39:13.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}长矛！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Spears!
Dialogue: 0,2:39:43.28,2:39:44.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}用长矛！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Use the spears!
Dialogue: 0,2:40:38.71,2:40:40.09,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你以为能把我们全杀了？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Thought you could kill us all?
Dialogue: 0,2:40:40.59,2:40:42.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}只要杀了你就够\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Long as I kill you.
Dialogue: 0,2:40:43.80,2:40:44.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}做个了断吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Finish this.
Dialogue: 0,2:40:48.01,2:40:49.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}父亲！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Dad!
Dialogue: 0,2:41:19.30,2:41:20.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}到了冥府\N{\rEN\blur0.8}When you get to Hades,
Dialogue: 0,2:41:22.80,2:41:26.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}告诉我的部下 我会西行 祭奠他们\N{\rEN\blur0.8}tell my men I will head west and honor them.
Dialogue: 0,2:41:32.47,2:41:33.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也告诉西农\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And tell Sinon
Dialogue: 0,2:41:36.27,2:41:38.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我把你的耻辱 还给你了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I gave you back your shame.
Dialogue: 0,2:41:58.04,2:41:59.42,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}怎么了？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What happened?
Dialogue: 0,2:42:00.59,2:42:01.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他赢了吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Did he beat them?
Dialogue: 0,2:42:03.05,2:42:04.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他死了吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Is he dead?
Dialogue: 0,2:42:06.17,2:42:08.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们打碎了人与人之间脆弱的纽带\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We broke the fragile bonds between men.
Dialogue: 0,2:42:17.52,2:42:20.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}此后数百年的黑暗岁月里\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And, for centuries of darkness to follow,
Dialogue: 0,2:42:20.69,2:42:24.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}特洛伊的故事 将只能靠歌谣流传……-\N{\rEN\blur0.8}the stories of Troy will only be sung...
Dialogue: 0,2:43:44.52,2:43:45.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}奥德修斯 我的爱人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Odysseus, my love.
Dialogue: 0,2:43:46.86,2:43:47.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}求求你 亲爱的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Please, my love.
Dialogue: 0,2:43:49.74,2:43:51.49,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}奥德修斯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Odysseus.
Dialogue: 0,2:43:51.57,2:43:53.99,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}亲爱的 你回来了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}My love. You came back.
Dialogue: 0,2:43:55.66,2:43:56.87,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}终于\N{\rEN\blur0.8}At last.
Dialogue: 0,2:43:57.58,2:43:58.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}在一切的尽头\N{\rEN\blur0.8}At the end.
Dialogue: 0,2:44:00.20,2:44:04.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}再看一眼 我心爱的伊萨卡\N{\rEN\blur0.8}To see my beloved Ithaca. One last time.
Dialogue: 0,2:44:05.21,2:44:06.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不 不\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No. No.
Dialogue: 0,2:44:06.80,2:44:07.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不 不 你不能这样 不能这样\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No, no, you can't. You can't.
Dialogue: 0,2:44:07.88,2:44:09.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不能这样 不能是现在 不能\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You can't. Not now. Not now.
Dialogue: 0,2:44:09.67,2:44:11.09,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}求求你 我已经等了太久\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Please. I've waited so long.
Dialogue: 0,2:44:13.55,2:44:14.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你不能死\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You can't die.
Dialogue: 0,2:44:16.18,2:44:17.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不是死亡\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Not death.
Dialogue: 0,2:44:19.31,2:44:20.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是流放\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Exile.
Dialogue: 0,2:44:28.86,2:44:30.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}忒勒马科斯会成为国王\N{\rEN\blur0.8}7elemachus will be King.
Dialogue: 0,2:44:34.28,2:44:36.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们会去往未知的西方\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We'll head into the unknown west.
Dialogue: 0,2:44:37.16,2:44:38.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}祭奠我的部下\N{\rEN\blur0.8}To honor my men.
Dialogue: 0,2:44:40.29,2:44:41.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一起去\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Together.
Dialogue: 0,2:44:42.04,2:44:43.87,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}乘上你最快的船·\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Take your fastest ship...
Dialogue: 0,2:44:44.62,2:44:46.67,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}带上你最聪慧的船员\N{\rEN\blur0.8}...and brightest crew.
Dialogue: 0,2:44:46.75,2:44:48.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}驶向地平线\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And head for the horizon.
Dialogue: 0,2:44:49.71,2:44:51.76,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}追逐西沉的太阳\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Chasing the escaping sun.
Dialogue: 0,2:44:51.84,2:44:54.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一张面孔\N{\rEN\blur0.8}A face...
Dialogue: 0,2:44:54.30,2:44:56.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}为什么故事只能靠歌谣流传？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Why will the stories only be sung?
Dialogue: 0,2:44:59.26,2:45:02.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}因为他们只能靠歌谣 记住曾经识字的我们\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Because songs will be all they have to remember those of us who could write.
Dialogue: 0,2:45:03.85,2:45:06.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一场战争……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}...a war...
Dialogue: 0,2:45:07.61,2:45:09.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}文明终将再度兴起\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Civilization will rise again.
Dialogue: 0,2:45:09.94,2:45:12.24,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一个男人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}...a man...
Dialogue: 0,2:45:15.86,2:45:18.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}新的黎明 将照亮黑暗的世界\N{\rEN\blur0.8}A new dawn will break over the darkened world.
Dialogue: 0,2:45:22.12,2:45:24.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}而我们犯下的错 将再次被遗忘\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And our mistakes will once again be forgotten.
Dialogue: 0,2:45:24.25,2:45:26.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}小条计策·\N{\rEN\blur0.8}...a trick...
Dialogue: 0,2:45:41.72,2:45:45.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}奥德赛
Dialogue: 0,2:45:47.15,2:45:49.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}编剧、导演 克里斯托弗 诺兰
Dialogue: 0,2:45:51.15,2:45:53.19,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}改编自荷马史诗 《奥德赛》
Dialogue: 0,2:45:54.82,2:45:56.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}制片人 艾玛 托马斯
Dialogue: 0,2:45:58.49,2:46:00.53,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}制片人 克里斯托弗 诺兰
Dialogue: 0,2:46:02.16,2:46:04.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}执行制片人 托马斯 海斯利普
Dialogue: 0,2:46:05.83,2:46:07.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}摄影指导 霍伊特 范 霍伊特玛
Dialogue: 0,2:46:09.50,2:46:11.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}美术指导 露丝 德容
Dialogue: 0,2:46:13.17,2:46:15.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}剪辑 詹妮弗 拉梅
Dialogue: 0,2:46:16.84,2:46:18.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}配乐 路德维希 戈兰松
Dialogue: 0,2:46:20.51,2:46:22.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}视觉特效总监 安德鲁 杰克逊
Dialogue: 0,2:46:24.18,2:46:26.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}实景特效总监 斯科特 R 费舍尔
Dialogue: 0,2:46:27.85,2:46:29.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}服装设计 艾伦 米罗伊尼克
Dialogue: 0,2:46:31.52,2:46:33.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}联合制片人 安迪 汤普森 ／海伦 梅德拉诺
Dialogue: 0,2:46:35.19,2:46:37.24,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}选角 约翰 帕普西德拉
Dialogue: 0,2:46:38.86,2:46:40.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}马特 达蒙
Dialogue: 0,2:46:42.53,2:46:44.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}汤姆 赫兰德
Dialogue: 0,2:46:46.20,2:46:48.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}安妮 海瑟薇
Dialogue: 0,2:46:49.88,2:46:51.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}罗伯特 帕丁森
Dialogue: 0,2:46:53.54,2:46:55.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}露皮塔 尼永奥
Dialogue: 0,2:46:57.22,2:46:59.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}萨曼莎 莫顿
Dialogue: 0,2:47:00.89,2:47:02.93,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}约翰 雷吉扎莫
Dialogue: 0,2:47:04.64,2:47:06.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}赞达亚
Dialogue: 0,2:47:08.31,2:47:10.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}查理兹 塞隆
Dialogue: 0,2:47:11.98,2:47:14.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}乔 博恩瑟／希米什 帕特尔
